module engine where

-- P1(a.6) sound-mode List classification.  Constructor names are scoped to
-- this module's global namespace, so keep the containment prefix explicit.
ContainmentListFace =
  TtClLive elem: TraversalType
  | TtClBlocked
  | TtClOther

-- containment — the type-level containment relation (set-algebra-to-fenel
-- Phase 6 capstone, Step 1). North-star: design/types-are-sets-and-the-
-- containment-substrate.md §4 ("the containment substrate — the Fenel-honest
-- shape"). Step-0 design + audit: workstreams/set-algebra-to-fenel/notes/
-- phase-6-step0-{A,B,C,D}-*.md; Step-1 probe verdict: notes/phase-6-step1-step0-probe.md.
--
-- The thesis: a type denotes the SET of its inhabitants, so type-level
-- containment IS the set operations. Containment is NOT a "Containable
-- typeclass" — it is plain functions over the `Type` universe (memory
-- [[feedback_typeclasses_are_types]]). Step 1 names the relation's `disjoint`
-- member by porting `type-algebra.ts:isDisjointType` (the legacy-TS STRUCTURAL
-- disjoint decider) to Fenel — the no-TS-principle "kill 2 birds": a
-- unification that retires legacy TS as it lands. The `subset` member (folding
-- the LIVE `engine:typeSubsumes`) is Step 2; `empty` + the component-wise
-- structural completion are Step 3.
--
-- ── How this folds the §2 layering ──────────────────────────────────────────
-- `isDisjointType` was already ONE containment decider with two modes:
-- STRUCTURAL (peel `$opaque.pure` / `$tagged.value`, compare shape tags) +
-- PREDICATE (at `$refined` / name-handle leaves, delegate to set-algebra's
-- `isDisjoint`). This port preserves that exact delegation — `disjoint` self-
-- reasons the structural frame and calls the already-Fenel predicate arm
-- (`set:decideDisjoint`, here resolved as bare `decideDisjoint` via the harness
-- slice) at the leaves. So set-algebra is RELOCATED as the predicate arm of one
-- named relation, not duplicated (north-star §6: "subsumption relocates").
--
-- ⚠ P1(a.8) UPDATES THE STRUCTURAL MODE ABOVE: the `$tagged.value` peel is
-- RETIRED IN SOUND MODE at all five sites (`t.dis.tagged` / `t.sub.tagged` /
-- `t.top.tagged` / `t.emp.tagged`) — the picker arms keep theirs. The paragraph
-- still describes the port's delegation correctly; only the tagged half of the
-- structural peel is gone.
--
-- ── Marshalling discipline (floor-kernel Phase 3c convergence) ──────────────
-- `disjoint`, `subset`, and `empty` now consume the SAME `TraversalType` tree.
-- The former `DisjointOperand` projection duplicated the `$`-key walk, carried
-- hierarchy pre-decisions from TS, and introduced unsound shape shortcuts
-- (`refined(Number,{1}) ⊥ Number` and `var a ⊥ Number` both returned Just true).
-- Phase 3c deletes that codec. `marshalTraversalType` is the sole mandatory
-- boundary; peeling, Boolean-former recursion, nominal-domain classification,
-- and every Tri decision below are Fenel-owned.

-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- disjoint — ⟦a⟧ ∩ ⟦b⟧ = ∅ ?  (Tri = Just true | Just false | Nothing)
-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- containment-substrate Phase 2 Step 1b — the tier-2 former arms (the folded
-- Phase-6 disjoint-lift) precede the leaf cascade: the structural "different
-- shape tags ⇒ disjoint" rule is UNSOUND for a union (it overlaps its branches'
-- shapes), so a union recurses component-wise (∧ — disjoint iff EVERY branch is),
-- type-substrate P1(a.5) — and that rule is now RETIRED for the LEAF cascade
-- too, not just for unions: see disjointLeaf. Distinct formers no longer prove
-- disjointness anywhere in this file.
-- an intersect ∃-wise (A∩B disjoint X if ANY branch is), complement
-- conservatively (Nothing). disjoint is commutative ⇒ a former on db reuses the
-- same combinators with da. The leaf cascade lives in disjointLeaf.
-- containment-substrate Phase 2.4 — between the former arms and the leaf cascade
-- sits the variant-vs-variant arm. P1(a.6 partitions exact Maybe forwarding
-- from the ordinary tagged face and gates every remaining tag/payload definite.
-- bothVariant still ensures every non-variant pair reaches the leaf cascade.

@label "Disjoint types"
@description "set-algebra-to-fenel Phase 6 / floor-kernel Phase 3c / type-substrate P1(a.5)+P1(a.6) — decide TraversalType disjointness. Void proves; opaque peels; the two `$tagged` peels are RETIRED and abstain (P1(a.8), `t.dis.tagged`); Boolean formers recurse; refined leaves keep only positive proofs. Exact Maybe is partitioned from ordinary tagged variants: exact/exact proves overlap only after eager-plan readiness, mixed pairs abstain, and ordinary variants require unique/default-discriminator plus keyed-product coordinate/occurrence gates before tag reasoning. Cross-former facts remain limited to unpeeled live host-carrier partitions."
@tags "engine" "containment" "disjoint" "type-algebra" "phase-6"
disjoint : (da: a) -> (db: a) -> Maybe Boolean
disjoint da db = disjointW false da db

-- ── type-substrate P1(a.5) round 2 — the OPAQUE-PEEL flag ───────────────────
-- `rp` = "a representation-changing wrapper was peeled to reach these operands".
-- WHY IT EXISTS. The leaf's carrier rules ask "which HOST VALUES does a former's
-- kind admit". That question is only answerable for a type as WRITTEN. `$opaque`
-- is precisely the wrapper whose job is to separate the conceptual `pure` ADT
-- from the runtime representation (the `Reprable` instance), so after peeling one
-- the KIND describes the pure view while the live membership faces reached
-- through the REGISTERED NAME describe the rep. ⚠ It is the NAME route (the
-- `Reprable` instance) that does this, NOT the `$opaque` node: MEASURED in the
-- committed differential, `{$ref:"Int"}` accepts 0/1/-1/… at both faces while a
-- RAW `$opaque{name="Int", pure=$record…}` written inline accepts NOTHING at
-- either face, because an ordinary opaque peel recurses through `pure`
-- (round 16). Three earlier versions of this line were wrong — one said EVERY
-- membership face describes the rep, one said every face of the registered
-- TOWER does, and one (this one, until round 18) offered the registered-NAME
-- route as the EVIDENCE that entitles `rp`.
--
-- ⚠ WHAT ACTUALLY ENTITLES `rp`, stated at round 18 because the face evidence
-- above is a SIBLING route and cannot carry it. The cells that actually reach
-- this peel are RAW `$opaque` nodes — `Int.opaque`, `Nat.opaque`, `Bool.opaque`
-- in the corpus — and those accept NOTHING at either measured face, so they
-- witness nothing either way. `rp` is entitled by the INTENDED `Reprable`
-- semantics (an `$opaque` is precisely the wrapper that separates the pure ADT
-- from the runtime representation, so a peel that forgets which one it is
-- looking at can decide the wrong population) plus the CONCRETE false cell
-- P1(a.5) measured before the flag existed. It is NOT entitled by what
-- `{$ref:"Int"}` accepts, and reading it that way is what would license the
-- blanket transplant to `ttTopCover` that rounds 10 and 12 REFUSED — losing the
-- sound `empty(¬$opaque{pure = Number}) = Just false`. `t.top.opaque`'s open question
-- is the narrower one of TOPNESS disagreement. MEASURED, and none of these is
-- exotic:
--   Int  = $opaque { pure = $record … }   inhabitants are host NUMBERS
--   Nat  = $opaque { pure = $variant … }  inhabitants are host NUMBERS
--   Bool = $opaque { pure = $variant … }  inhabitants are host BOOLEANS
--   List = $opaque { pure = $variant … }  inhabitants are host ARRAYS
-- so `disjoint({$ref:"Number"}, Nat)` reached `named × variant` and answered
-- `Just true` while every natural number inhabits BOTH. This is the SAME
-- "the kind does not fix the carrier" argument that removed `$map` from the
-- allow-lists — it just applies to every kind once a peel is involved.
-- `$refined` does NOT set it: a refinement of Number is still numbers.
-- `$tagged` does not set it either, and the reason is now simply that IT NO
-- LONGER PEELS HERE — P1(a.8) retired both tagged peels in `disjointW`, so
-- there is no tagged reveal for `rp` to model.  ⚠ Two earlier justifications
-- written on this line were FALSE and are recorded so neither is restored:
-- "a phantom tag erases to its value slot" (the VALUE-RECURSION reading stated
-- as fact) and "a phantom tag does not swap the host carrier".  The second is
-- refuted by measurement: `validate(Number, 5)` succeeds while
-- `validate(Tag(Number), 5)` fails, and `validate(Tag(Number), <uuid>)`
-- succeeds while `validate(Number, <uuid>)` fails — the tag DOES swap the live
-- carrier, from numbers to UUID strings.  `$opaque` is the only peel LEFT here
-- that swaps the carrier, which is a fact about the surviving peels and not a
-- claim that tagging preserves it.
-- WHERE THE FLAG TRAVELS, corrected by the round-3 review: union and intersect
-- branches KEEP it. The first version reset them on the reasoning that "a union
-- branch is a written type in its own right" — true of a top-level union, FALSE
-- of one that is a peeled `$opaque`'s own `pure` view, where the opaque's
-- representation still transports every branch. Propagating an already-set flag
-- can only add abstentions, never remove one: a top-level union arrives with
-- rp already false. Payload FIELDS still reset, and that is deliberate — a
-- field's type carries its own `Reprable`, independent of its container's.
@label "disjoint: disjointW"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.5) — the representation-peel-aware core of disjoint. Threads `rp`, set when an `$opaque` wrapper has been peeled to reach the current operands, and consumes it wherever a carrier-sensitive verdict could otherwise escape: the two host-carrier rules at the leaf (ttHostSortExclusive / ttNamedSortExclusive), `disjointNonFormer`'s tag arm (disjointVariant, whose constructor-tag rule is a claim about the PURE ADT), and both `$complement` handoffs to `subsetW`. None may decide a peeled operand: `$opaque` separates the pure ADT from the runtime representation, so after the peel the kind describes `pure` while the operand's live population is the REP's. ⚠ ROUND 20: what entitles `rp` is the INTENDED `Reprable` semantics plus the concrete false cell P1(a.5) measured — NOT the face behaviour of the registered NAME route, which is a SIBLING. The raw `$opaque` nodes that actually reach this peel (`Int.opaque` / `Nat.opaque` / `Bool.opaque` in the corpus) accept NOTHING at either measured face and witness nothing either way, and an INLINE `$opaque{pure=Number}` recurses into `pure` at both. Reading the name route as the evidence is what would license the blanket transplant to `ttTopCover` that rounds 10 and 12 REFUSED, losing the sound `empty(¬$opaque{pure = Number}) = Just false` (Int peels to $record but holds numbers; Nat/Bool/List peel to $variant but hold numbers/booleans/arrays). In particular, a peeled operand no longer describes the live carrier, and `subsetW` has no representation flag with which to justify the complement reduction, so those arms abstain when `rp` is set. `$refined` peels do NOT set it — a refinement does not change the carrier. **type-substrate P1(a.8): the two `$tagged` peels are RETIRED — BOTH operand orders now abstain unconditionally (ledger `t.dis.tagged`), and they are SEPARATELY REACHABLE arms: the LEFT peel fires when the left operand is `$tagged` AND no earlier arm has already decided — the void checks sit above both peels, so `dis(Tag(Number), $void)` is `Just true` at the void check and never reaches the peel — so the RIGHT peel is reached only when the left is not tagged, and a census of left-operand cells pins one of the two fences. Ground: validation reads a `$tagged` by UUID syntax only while `matchesShape` recurses into the value slot, so `<uuid>` is admitted by every `$tagged` type and a \"disjoint\" pair CAN share a live witness. The cell where that actually bites is `dis(Tag($void), Tag($void))` — both operands admit `<uuid>` while value-recursion makes both empty, so the two readings disagree and the arm must abstain. The MIXED cells are NOT contradictions and are PRICED rather than repaired: `<uuid>` does not validate against `Number` (MEASURED), so `dis(Tag($void), Number)` is disjoint under both readings. MEASURED at entry: `dis(Tag($void), Tag($void))`, `dis(Tag($void), Number)` and `dis(Number, Tag($void))` were all `Just true`.** The union and intersect arms THREAD the flag rather than resetting it (round 4); every remaining arm retains its pre-round-4 logic (the leaf and tag arms did change when `rp` was introduced, so \"byte-identical to the pre-flag body\" is NOT the right claim about them). Internal core."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "type-substrate" "phase-1a5"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointW : (rp: Boolean) -> (da: a) -> (db: a) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointW rp da db =
  if tsIsVoid da then Just true
  else if tsIsVoid db then Just true
  else if eq (tsKind da) "opaque" then disjointW true (tsPure da) db
  else if eq (tsKind db) "opaque" then disjointW true da (tsPure db)
  else if eq (tsKind da) "tagged" then Nothing
  else if eq (tsKind db) "tagged" then Nothing
  else if eq (tsKind da) "union" then disjointUnion rp (tsUnionBranches da) db
  else if eq (tsKind da) "intersect" then disjointIntersectOp rp (tsIntersectBranches da) db
  else if eq (tsKind da) "complement" then if rp then Nothing else subsetW false db (tsComplementInner da)
  else if eq (tsKind db) "union" then disjointUnion rp (tsUnionBranches db) da
  else if eq (tsKind db) "intersect" then disjointIntersectOp rp (tsIntersectBranches db) da
  else if eq (tsKind db) "complement" then if rp then Nothing else subsetW false da (tsComplementInner db)
  else disjointNonFormer rp da db

-- disjointNonFormer — the non-former tail of disjoint (Phase 2.4): two $variants
-- decide by tag (disjointVariant); everything else hits the unchanged leaf
-- cascade. Split out so disjoint's former chain stays under the per-decl token cap
-- (the Step-2 Fenel-parser fence). byte-identity of every non-variant decision.
@label "disjoint: disjointNonFormer"
@description "Phase 2.4 / floor-kernel Phase 3c / type-substrate P1(a.5)+P1(a.6) — two unpeeled variants enter disjointVariant's exact-Maybe/ordinary partition and face gates; everything else uses the sound leaf cascade. After an opaque peel, tags describe the pure ADT rather than the live carrier, so variant pairs abstain."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointNonFormer : (rp: Boolean) -> (da: a) -> (db: a) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointNonFormer rp da db =
  if and (bothVariant da db) (not rp) then disjointVariant da db
  else disjointLeaf rp da db

-- disjointLeaf — sound leaf cascade over TraversalType. Refined types are
-- subsets of their base, so only a positive predicate/base disjoint proof may
-- escape; a proven overlap of the two predicate sets is NOT enough to prove the
-- refined intersections overlap. This fixes the legacy refined-vs-base lie.
--
-- ── type-substrate P1(a.5) — the FORMER-AS-SORT model, RETRACTED ────────────
-- The rigid arm used to read "distinct rigid former ⇒ Just true disjoint". That
-- was a PRODUCER claim promoted to a claim about the host-value universe — the
-- exact error P1(a) retracted one core over (`dis.arrow.ctor`: "a callable
-- carries no `$tag`"). Formers are not sorts: the FACES decide which host values
-- inhabit a type, and there the object formers overlap freely. MEASURED shared
-- witnesses. The FACE is named per cell because two of them degrade: matchesShape
-- has NO arrow arm (`_ -> true`, an unimplemented ACCEPT) and validate routes
-- `$tuple`/`$unit` into one refuse-all — neither is evidence, in either direction.
--   record{} ∩ variant P{}  ∋ {$tag:"P"}               matchesShape AND validate
--   record{} ∩ arrow        ∋ {__fenelFn:…}            validate (both sides)
--   record{} ∩ map          ∋ {}                       matchesShape AND validate
--   record{} ∩ unit         ∋ {}                       matchesShape (unit's only
--                                                      implemented face)
--   variant  ∩ map          ∋ {$tag:"P"}               matchesShape
--   variant  ∩ arrow        ∋ {$tag:"P",__fenelFn:…}   validate (both sides) — the
--                                                      8λ.1 CHIMERA, live here; bare
--                                                      {$tag:"P"} is NOT an arrow
--   map      ∩ tuple        ∋ [1,2,3]                  validate(Vec(Number,3)) — a
--                                                      $map over Fin 3 takes ARRAYS —
--                                                      and matchesShape(tuple[N,N,N])
--   map      ∩ unit / arrow ∋ {}                       matchesShape / validate
-- The former P1(a.5) DERIVED claim for variant ∩ unit was false: exact
-- Maybe(Unit) forwards `{}` to Unit, so `{}` inhabits both at the measured
-- membership face. The cell remains failed closed on measured evidence.
-- Only `ttHostSortExclusive` survives: `tuple` (an ARRAY at its one real arm)
-- against record / unit, which every implemented face refuses arrays for, and
-- only on an UN-PEELED operand pair. `arrow`, `map` and — since round 2 —
-- `variant` are NEVER exclusive; see that helper's comment for each reason.
-- The posture is FAIL-CLOSED, not twin-precision: Tt ABSTAINS where its rule was
-- refuted (`variant P{} ⊆ record{}` is genuinely TRUE and the Se core proves it;
-- Tt does not, on purpose). Recovering that precision is convergence work.
@label "disjoint: disjointLeaf"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c / type-substrate P1(a.5) — sound TraversalType leaf disjointness: refined leaves accept only positive set/base disjoint proofs; named pairs use Fenel-owned domain classification (and exact-name inhabitance for Just false); a named atom is disjoint from a rigid former only on the host sorts that former genuinely refuses (ttNamedSortExclusive); two rigid formers are disjoint only when their host carriers are exclusive (ttHostSortExclusive — the Array.isArray partition, `tuple` vs `record`/`unit`). BOTH rules additionally require rp = false (no `$opaque` peel). Every other cross-kind pair, and variables/unknowns/aliases, abstain. The former-as-sort model is RETRACTED: distinct formers no longer prove disjointness. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointLeaf : (rp: Boolean) -> (da: a) -> (db: a) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointLeaf rp da db =
  if eq (tsKind da) "refined" then disjointRefined rp da db
  else if eq (tsKind db) "refined" then disjointRefined rp db da
  else if eq (tsKind da) "named" then disjointNamed rp da db
  else if eq (tsKind db) "named" then disjointNamed rp db da
  else if and (ttRigidKind (tsKind da)) (ttRigidKind (tsKind db))
    then if and (not rp) (ttHostSortExclusive (tsKind da) (tsKind db)) then Just true else Nothing
    else Nothing

@label "disjoint: refined"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — refined r=base∩set is disjoint from another refined when their predicate sets OR their bases are provably disjoint; against any other type, a positive base-disjoint proof suffices. emTrueOnly deliberately drops Just false: overlapping predicates/bases do not prove the intersections inhabited. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "refined" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointRefined : (rp: Boolean) -> (r: a) -> (other: a) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointRefined rp r other =
  if eq (tsKind other) "refined"
  then mOr (emTrueOnly (decideDisjoint (tsRefinedSet r) (tsRefinedSet other))) (emTrueOnly (disjointW rp (tsBase r) (tsBase other)))
  else emTrueOnly (disjointW rp (tsBase r) other)

@label "disjoint: named"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c / type-substrate P1(a.5) — named-leaf disjointness. Two names: exact known-inhabited name ⇒ Just false; otherwise differing known value domains ⇒ Just true. A known atomic name is disjoint from a rigid former only where that former's live membership genuinely refuses the atom's host sort (ttNamedSortExclusive): `map` refuses nothing (its key domain is unresolved at the leaf — Fin-n maps take arrays, locale maps take strings, enum-keyed maps accept identically) and `arrow` accepts fnId STRINGS, so String-vs-arrow and every atom-vs-map pair now abstain. Unknown names and array-domain aliases abstain. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "named" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointNamed : (rp: Boolean) -> (named: a) -> (other: a) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointNamed rp named other =
  if eq (tsKind other) "named"
  then containmentNamedPair (tsName named) (tsName other)
  else if ttRigidKind (tsKind other)
    then if and (not rp) (ttNamedSortExclusive (tsName named) (tsKind other)) then Just true else Nothing
    else Nothing

@label "disjoint: namedPair"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — decide a named pair from exact-name inhabitance or differing value domains. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "named" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
containmentNamedPair : (a: String) -> (b: String) -> Maybe Boolean
containmentNamedPair a b =
  if eq a b
  then case emptyNamed a of
    Just false -> Just false
    _ -> Nothing
  else setAlgebraNamedDisjoint (containmentNamedDomain a) (containmentNamedDomain b)

@label "disjoint: namedDomain"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — registry-backed named value-domain classification with no TS hierarchy flag: String descendants (including str:*) ⇒ string; Bool/Boolean ⇒ boolean; Number descendants ⇒ number; residual format/list/multiple prefixes use the shared Fenel classifier; char:* remains unknown because it accepts both codepoint numbers and one-character strings. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "named" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
containmentNamedDomain : (name: String) -> Maybe a
containmentNamedDomain name =
  if elem name ["Rational", "ℚ", "Nat", "ℕ", "Int", "ℤ"] then Nothing
  else if startsWith name "char:" then Nothing
  else if namedSubsetCheck name "String" then Just (NdString)
  else if eq name "Bool" then Just (NdBoolean)
  else if eq name "Boolean" then Just (NdBoolean)
  else if namedSubsetCheck name "Number" then Just (NdNumber)
  else setAlgebraNamedDomainFromName name

@label "disjoint: atomicNamed"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — true when a named domain is one of the scalar atom sorts (number/string/boolean); array and unknown domains do not justify a named-vs-structural disjoint claim. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "named" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
containmentAtomicNamed : (name: String) -> Boolean
containmentAtomicNamed name = case containmentNamedDomain name of
  Just NdNumber -> true
  Just NdString -> true
  Just NdBoolean -> true
  _ -> false

@label "disjoint: rigidKind"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c / type-substrate P1(a.5) — the closed structural former kinds. Excludes named/refined/var/mu/app/other because aliases, recursion, or unknown denotations can cross shapes. NOTE: membership of this set no longer implies anything about disjointness — the former-as-sort model was RETRACTED; it now only marks that a closed structural former was written here, gating ttHostSortExclusive / ttNamedSortExclusive (which decide) and ttTopCover's not-the-universe arm. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttRigidKind : (k: String) -> Boolean
ttRigidKind k =
  if eq k "record" then true
  else if eq k "variant" then true
  else if eq k "tuple" then true
  else if eq k "map" then true
  else if eq k "arrow" then true
  else eq k "unit"

-- ── type-substrate P1(a.5) — the surviving host-carrier partitions ──────────
-- ROUND-2 NARROWING, and read this before widening anything back. Two of the
-- kinds originally admitted here were removed after a result-review round
-- MEASURED them false, both for the same reason the `$map` exclusion below
-- already gives — THE KIND DOES NOT FIX THE CARRIER:
--   `variant` — canonical `Maybe` is a bare `$variant` (no wrapper at all) and
--     `validationValidateMaybe` FORWARDS a non-null untagged value to its inner
--     type, returning it unchanged. So `42` inhabits `Maybe Number` and `[1]`
--     inhabits `Maybe (List Number)`, and `disjoint(Number, Maybe Number)` and
--     `disjoint(Maybe (List Number), $tuple[Number])` were both `Just true`.
--     A `$variant` kind therefore does NOT imply tagged-object membership.
--   every kind, once an `$opaque` has been PEELED — see `disjointW`'s `rp` flag.
--     `List` is `$opaque` over a `$variant` and holds ARRAYS; `Int` is `$opaque`
--     over a `$record` and holds NUMBERS. The flag, not this table, closes that.
-- The ONE axis a Tt cross-kind definite may cite: `Array.isArray`. `tuple` is
-- the only rigid former whose sole implemented membership arm REQUIRES an array
-- (decompose.fenel:decomposeMatchesTuple wants a DcvArray of the declared
-- length; its validate arm is the VtOther refuse-all, i.e. a degrade, and its Se
-- projection is the keyless `SeAll` degrade — neither may be cited). Against it:
--   record  — decomposeMatchesRecord wants a DcvObject; validationValidateRecord
--             wants validationIsRecord (which excludes isArray); Se's SeCtor
--             refutes arrays. THREE implemented refusals. EXCLUSIVE.
--   unit    — decomposeMatchesUnit takes only DcvNull or an EMPTY DcvObject, and
--             marshalDcValue routes every array to the separate DcvArray case,
--             so an array can never reach it. ONE implemented face, but closed.
--             EXCLUSIVE (pin the `[]` witness — it is the thin one).
-- NOT exclusive, both MEASURED, both deliberately absent below:
--   map     — the kind does not fix the carrier. `Vec(Number,3)` IS `$map` over
--             `Fin 3` and validate ACCEPTS `[1,2,3]` identically; locale maps
--             accept bare strings; enum-keyed maps accept anything. A kind-level
--             rule must hold for EVERY key domain, and none does.
--   arrow   — arrowhood is a MARKER on a plain host object, not a host sort:
--             json-logic.ts isClosure/isPartial/isRef test `typeof === "object"`
--             plus a key and NEVER consult Array.isArray, so `Object.assign([],
--             {$ref:"f"})` is callable at the engine's own application gate.
--             validate's array refusal is validationIsRecord POLICY and Se's is
--             the same convention re-encoded — one convention counted twice, not
--             two witnesses, and the engine does not enforce it.
-- Recovery is by ENFORCEMENT, not argument: if the callable gate ever gains an
-- Array.isArray exclusion, arrow becomes genuinely closed on this axis and the
-- cell can be re-admitted WITH a pin. Do not re-admit it by re-reading validate.
@label "disjoint: hostSortExclusive"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.5) — the ONLY surviving rigid-former disjointness rule: two rigid kinds are disjoint iff their live membership carriers are mutually exclusive on a host-value classification axis. Exactly the Array.isArray partition — `tuple` (array-only at its one implemented arm) against `record` / `unit` (each of which every implemented face refuses arrays for) — and its callers additionally require an UN-PEELED operand pair (disjointW's rp flag). `map`, `arrow` and `variant` are NEVER exclusive with anything: a $map's carrier depends on its unresolved key domain (Fin-n gives arrays, locale gives strings, enum accepts everything); arrowhood is a marker on a plain object that the engine's own callable gate reads without consulting Array.isArray; and canonical Maybe is a bare $variant whose validate arm FORWARDS an untagged value to its inner type, so a $variant kind implies nothing about the carrier either. Symmetric, and false on equal kinds (same-kind pairs coarsen elsewhere). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "subset" "type-substrate" "phase-1a5"
@category "engine-internal"
ttHostSortExclusive : (ka: String) -> (kb: String) -> Boolean
ttHostSortExclusive ka kb =
  if eq ka "tuple" then ttArrayExclusiveKind kb
  else if eq kb "tuple" then ttArrayExclusiveKind ka
  else false

@label "disjoint: arrayExclusiveKind"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.5) — the rigid former kinds whose every IMPLEMENTED membership arm refuses host arrays, so a tuple (array-only) cannot share a value with them: record and unit, and ONLY on an un-peeled operand (see disjointW's rp flag). Deliberately excludes `map` (Fin-n key domains denote arrays — Vec(Number,3) is a $map and validate accepts [1,2,3]), `arrow` (the engine's callable gate accepts a decorated array), and — round 2 — `variant`, because canonical Maybe FORWARDS an untagged value to its inner type at the validate face, so a $variant kind does not imply tagged-object membership. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "type-substrate" "phase-1a5"
@category "engine-internal"
ttArrayExclusiveKind : (k: String) -> Boolean
ttArrayExclusiveKind k =
  if eq k "record" then true
  else eq k "unit"

-- ── type-substrate P1(a.5) — the named-atom / former partition, narrowed ────
-- `containmentAtomicNamed` still says WHICH names denote a scalar host sort;
-- what changed is that scalar-hood alone no longer proves disjointness from a
-- former, because two formers accept scalars at REAL arms:
--   arrow accepts a fnId STRING — validationValidateArrow's `isString` branch is
--     an IDENTITY accept (`validationOk value`) that looks the name up and checks
--     arity + signature subtype; `maybeFunctor.fmap = "algebra:maybeFmap"` is a
--     live instance of exactly that. Se's arrow face ABSTAINS on strings rather
--     than refuting, so nothing underwrites the definite either.
--   map accepts a string through the locale arm and ANY value through the
--     enum-key arm, both identity accepts.
-- Number/Boolean survive against every former EXCEPT map: `typeof` is closed
-- there at every implemented face AND at the callable gate (isClosure requires
-- `typeof === "object"`, so a raw number can never be a callable).
-- EVIDENCE RULE used throughout, and worth keeping: `validationOk value`
-- (IDENTITY) is membership evidence; `validationOk (f value)` is a COERCION and
-- is not. That is why validate(String, 42) = valid is NOT a counterexample to
-- the scalar partition — validationValidateString returns a COERCED value.
@label "disjoint: namedSortExclusive"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.5) — is a named atom's host sort exclusive with a rigid former's live membership carrier? A scalar atom (number/string/boolean per containmentAtomicNamed) is exclusive with every rigid former EXCEPT: `map`, whose enum-key arm accepts any value identically and whose locale arm accepts bare strings, and — for String only — `arrow`, whose validate arm identity-accepts a fnId string (the Ref substrate's Codeable projection) while the Se arrow face merely abstains. Non-atomic names (array/unknown domains) never justify the claim. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "named" "type-substrate" "phase-1a5"
@category "engine-internal"
ttNamedSortExclusive : (name: String) -> (k: String) -> Boolean
ttNamedSortExclusive name k =
  if not (containmentAtomicNamed name) then false
  else if eq k "map" then false
  else if eq k "variant" then false
  else if eq k "arrow" then not (containmentStringNamed name)
  else ttRigidKind k

@label "disjoint: stringNamed"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.5) — true when a named domain is the STRING scalar sort. Split out because the string sort is the one atom an `$arrow` genuinely accepts (a fnId name), so it is the one exclusion ttNamedSortExclusive must make on the arrow column. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "named" "type-substrate" "phase-1a5"
@category "engine-internal"
containmentStringNamed : (name: String) -> Boolean
containmentStringNamed name = case containmentNamedDomain name of
  Just NdString -> true
  _ -> false

-- ── helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- containmentProven — isJustTrue: is the Tri a `Just true` (a positive proof)?
@label "containment: proven"
@description "Phase 6 Step 1 — isJustTrue over a Tri (Maybe Bool): `Just true` ⇒ true, `Just false`/`Nothing` ⇒ false. Internal helper to disjoint (the `return true` short-circuit gate). Mirrors maybe-bool.ts:isJustTrue."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
containmentProven : (m: a) -> Boolean
containmentProven m = case m of
  Just b -> b
  Nothing -> false

-- containmentConservative — the same-shape, no-positive-proof fall-through. The
-- honest Tri (decision C-1): a check-1 `Just false` (a leaf PROVEN non-disjoint)
-- ⇒ Just false; else Nothing. Both collapse to `false` under the Bool boundary,
-- so isJustTrue is byte-equal to `isDisjointType`'s conservative `false`.
@label "containment: conservative"
@description "Phase 6 Step 1 — the same-shape no-positive-proof fall-through of disjoint: a check-1 Just false (a leaf proven NON-disjoint) ⇒ Just false (honest Tri, decision C-1); else Nothing. Both collapse to false under the Bool boundary (isDisjointType's conservative false). Internal helper to disjoint."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
containmentConservative : (c1: a) -> Maybe Boolean
containmentConservative c1 = case c1 of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b -> if b then Nothing else Just false

-- P1(a.6) keeps only positive recursive facts where wrapping can erase a
-- negative witness.
@category "engine-internal"
ttKeepTrue : (m: Maybe Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
ttKeepTrue m = case m of
  Just true -> Just true
  _ -> Nothing

@category "engine-internal"
ttExactMaybeInner : (t: a) -> Maybe b
ttExactMaybeInner t = case t of
  TtVariant { cases = cases } -> typeTraversalMaybeInner cases
  _ -> Nothing

-- One registry-scoped projection row.  Positional fields are already complete
-- in TraversalType; NamedField is the only host lookup.
@category "engine-internal"
ttSlotProjection : (slot: a) -> Maybe b
ttSlotProjection slot = case slot.semanticKey of
  PositionalField ->
    if eq slot.wireName ""
    then Nothing
    else Just { key = slot.semanticKey, embeddedWire = slot.wireName, effectiveWire = slot.wireName, widgetName = "", occurrenceType = slot.type }
  NamedField -> ttNamedSlotProjection slot (fieldKeyValidationProjection slot.semanticKey)

@category "engine-internal"
ttNamedSlotProjection : (slot: a) -> (projection: Maybe b) -> Maybe c
ttNamedSlotProjection slot projection = case projection of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just p ->
    if eq p.wireName ""
    then Nothing
    else Just { key = slot.semanticKey, embeddedWire = slot.wireName, effectiveWire = p.wireName, widgetName = p.widgetName, occurrenceType = slot.type }

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectSlots : (slots: List a) -> Maybe (List b)
ttProjectSlots slots = ttProjectSlotsFrom slots []

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectSlotsFrom : (slots: List a) -> (acc: List b) -> Maybe (List b)
ttProjectSlotsFrom slots acc = case head slots of
  Nothing -> Just acc
  Just slot -> case ttSlotProjection slot of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just row -> ttProjectSlotsFrom (ssRest slots) (appendItem row acc)

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedEffectiveSlots : (rows: List a) -> List b
ttProjectedEffectiveSlots rows = map (\row -> { key = row.key, wireName = row.effectiveWire }) rows

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedChildrenPlanReady : (rows: List a) -> Boolean
ttProjectedChildrenPlanReady rows = case head rows of
  Nothing -> true
  Just row -> if ttValidationPlanReady row.occurrenceType then ttProjectedChildrenPlanReady (ssRest rows) else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedChildrenOccurrenceReady : (rows: List a) -> Boolean
ttProjectedChildrenOccurrenceReady rows = case head rows of
  Nothing -> true
  Just row ->
    if validationWidgetSkipsOccurrence row.widgetName
    then false
    else if ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady row.occurrenceType then ttProjectedChildrenOccurrenceReady (ssRest rows) else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttSlotsPlanReady : (slots: List a) -> Boolean
ttSlotsPlanReady slots = case ttProjectSlots slots of
  Nothing -> false
  Just rows ->
    if fieldSemanticSlotsValid (ttProjectedEffectiveSlots rows)
    then ttProjectedChildrenPlanReady rows
    else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttCasesPlanReady : (cases: List a) -> Boolean
ttCasesPlanReady cases = case head cases of
  Nothing -> true
  Just variantCase -> if ttSlotsPlanReady variantCase.fields then ttCasesPlanReady (ssRest cases) else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttVariantPlanReady : (cases: List a) -> Boolean
ttVariantPlanReady cases = case typeTraversalMaybeInner cases of
  Just inner -> ttValidationPlanReady inner
  Nothing -> ttCasesPlanReady cases

-- This mirrors validation's eager planning shape and gates whether a structural
-- verdict may be LIFTED to a definite.  P1(a.6) made both tails FAIL-CLOSED: the
-- old `_ -> true` admitted every former validation elaborates to `VtOther`
-- (non-List mu / unit / void / tuple / union / intersect / complement / unknown),
-- and `VtOther` REFUSES every value (validate.fenel:1577) without being a plan
-- error (validationTypePlanError's tail is `_ -> Nothing`, validate.fenel:1105).
-- Two false definites rode that gap: `List(U1) ⊆ List(U2)` for distinct unions
-- returned `Just false` though both populations are exactly {[]} at validate and
-- all-arrays at matchesShape, and `List(Nat) ⊆ List(Nat ∪ Bool)` returned
-- `Just true` though `[1]` is refused on the want side.
-- `TtVoid` is the ONE `VtOther` former that stays ADMITTED, because for `$void`
-- alone the refuse-every-value plan IS the faithful denotation: ⟦$void⟧ = ∅, and
-- a plan that refuses everything denotes exactly ∅.  For `TtUnion` / `TtTuple` /
-- `TtUnit` / non-List `TtMu` the same refusal is a LIE about a nonempty
-- denotation, which is what made it unsound.  Admitting Void keeps the sound
-- vacuity proofs (`record{x: $void}` really is empty at both faces, so
-- `∅ ⊆ anything` and the emptiness folds stay definite).
-- The exact derived universal type `complement Void` is now also ready:
-- validationElaborateType recognizes that identity and accepts every value
-- without coercion. No other complement inherits that support.
-- `TtArrow` and `TtMap` are excluded for the same reason at a different axis:
-- validationValidateArrow accepts "", accepts any UNKNOWN function name, and
-- accepts every lambda/partial signature-blind (validate.fenel:1521-1535), so an
-- arrow variance/arity refutation is separated only if the mutable function-fact
-- registry happens to contain a separating name; and validationValidateMap is
-- key-blind in both non-finite branches (validate.fenel:1500-1510) while ssMap
-- emits key-domain definites.  Top-level ssMap / arrowSub / tupleSub / ssApp
-- were NOT gated by this predicate and kept that exposure; type-substrate
-- P1(a.7) CLOSED it at the source instead of by a consult here — arrow, map and
-- app abstain outright and tuple is positive-only, so no unentitled top-level
-- composite definite survives.  A consult on those three arms would have been an
-- UNEXERCISABLE branch, because this predicate answers `false` unconditionally
-- for TtArrow, TtMap and (via the tail) TtTuple.  Restoring any of them is a
-- future readiness phase's job, WITH tests, once a ready former exists to test
-- against; see ssCompositeSound and the tcb-ledger rows.
-- KEEP THIS CASE LIST PARALLEL TO ttOccurrenceEnforcing's.  Divergence is a real
-- bug class: TtNamed was present here and MISSING there, so fail-closing the
-- tails alone would have occurrence-fenced every primitive leaf.
@category "engine-internal"
ttValidationPlanReady : (t: a) -> Boolean
ttValidationPlanReady t = case t of
  TtRefined { base = base } -> ttValidationPlanReady base
  TtNamed { name = name } -> validationPrimitiveName name
  TtRecord { fields = fields } -> ttSlotsPlanReady fields
  TtVariant { cases = cases } -> ttVariantPlanReady cases
  TtVoid {} -> true
  TtComplement { inner = inner } -> case inner of TtVoid {} -> true; _ -> false
  TtMap {} -> false
  TtArrow {} -> false
  _ -> ttValidationPlanReadyTail t

@category "engine-internal"
ttValidationPlanReadyTail : (t: a) -> Boolean
ttValidationPlanReadyTail t = case t of
  TtOpaque { pure = pure } -> case validationListInner t of
    Just elem -> ttValidationPlanReady elem
    Nothing -> ttValidationPlanReady pure
  TtMu {} -> case validationListInner t of
    Just elem -> ttValidationPlanReady elem
    Nothing -> false
  _ -> false

@category "engine-internal"
ttSlotsOccurrenceEnforcing : (slots: List a) -> Boolean
ttSlotsOccurrenceEnforcing slots = case ttProjectSlots slots of
  Nothing -> false
  Just rows -> ttProjectedChildrenOccurrenceReady rows

@category "engine-internal"
ttCasesOccurrenceReady : (cases: List a) -> Boolean
ttCasesOccurrenceReady cases = case head cases of
  Nothing -> true
  Just variantCase -> if ttSlotsOccurrenceEnforcing variantCase.fields then ttCasesOccurrenceReady (ssRest cases) else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttVariantOccurrenceReady : (cases: List a) -> Boolean
ttVariantOccurrenceReady cases = case typeTraversalMaybeInner cases of
  Just inner -> ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady inner
  Nothing -> ttCasesOccurrenceReady cases

@category "engine-internal"
ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady : (t: a) -> Boolean
ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady t =
  if ttValidationPlanReady t then ttOccurrenceEnforcing t else false

-- The occurrence twin of ttValidationPlanReady.  P1(a.6) added the TtNamed arm
-- (it was absent, riding the old `_ -> true` tail) and fail-closed both tails, so
-- the two case lists now match arm for arm.  Adding a former to one REQUIRES
-- adding it to the other; the named-arm parity pin enforces it executably.
@category "engine-internal"
ttOccurrenceEnforcing : (t: a) -> Boolean
ttOccurrenceEnforcing t = case t of
  TtRefined { base = base } -> ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady base
  TtNamed { name = name } -> validationPrimitiveName name
  TtRecord { fields = fields } -> ttSlotsOccurrenceEnforcing fields
  TtVariant { cases = cases } -> ttVariantOccurrenceReady cases
  TtVoid {} -> true
  TtComplement { inner = inner } -> case inner of TtVoid {} -> true; _ -> false
  TtMap {} -> false
  TtArrow {} -> false
  _ -> ttOccurrenceEnforcingTail t

@category "engine-internal"
ttOccurrenceEnforcingTail : (t: a) -> Boolean
ttOccurrenceEnforcingTail t = case t of
  TtOpaque { pure = pure } -> case validationListInner t of
    Just elem -> ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady elem
    Nothing -> ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady pure
  TtMu {} -> case validationListInner t of
    Just elem -> ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady elem
    Nothing -> false
  _ -> false

-- Single- and paired-product face fences.  The existing semantic-slot helper
-- owns validity/injectivity; these helpers add scoped projection, reserved
-- coordinates, widget enforcement, and cross-operand alignment.
@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedReservedFree : (rows: List a) -> Boolean
ttProjectedReservedFree rows = case head rows of
  Nothing -> true
  Just row ->
    if or (eq row.embeddedWire "$tag") (eq row.embeddedWire "__case")
    then false
    else ttProjectedReservedFree (ssRest rows)

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedDiscriminatorFree : (active: String) -> (rows: List a) -> Boolean
ttProjectedDiscriminatorFree active rows =
  if eq active "" then true else ttProjectedDiscriminatorFreeW active rows

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedDiscriminatorFreeW : (active: String) -> (rows: List a) -> Boolean
ttProjectedDiscriminatorFreeW active rows = case head rows of
  Nothing -> true
  Just row -> if eq row.effectiveWire active then false else ttProjectedDiscriminatorFreeW active (ssRest rows)

@category "engine-internal"
ttProductSingleReady : (fields: List a) -> (active: String) -> Boolean
ttProductSingleReady fields active = case ttProjectSlots fields of
  Nothing -> false
  Just rows -> ttProductSingleProjectedReady fields active rows

@category "engine-internal"
ttProductSingleProjectedReady : (fields: List a) -> (active: String) -> (rows: List b) -> Boolean
ttProductSingleProjectedReady fields active rows =
  if not (fieldSemanticSlotsValid (typeTraversalSemanticFieldProjections fields)) then false
  else if not (fieldSemanticSlotsValid (ttProjectedEffectiveSlots rows)) then false
  else if not (ttProjectedReservedFree rows) then false
  else if not (ttProjectedDiscriminatorFree active rows) then false
  else ttProjectedChildrenOccurrenceReady rows

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedFindKey : (rows: List a) -> (key: b) -> Maybe a
ttProjectedFindKey rows key = case head rows of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just row -> if fieldKeyEq row.key key then Just row else ttProjectedFindKey (ssRest rows) key

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedFindEmbedded : (rows: List a) -> (wireName: String) -> Maybe a
ttProjectedFindEmbedded rows wireName = case head rows of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just row -> if eq row.embeddedWire wireName then Just row else ttProjectedFindEmbedded (ssRest rows) wireName

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedFindEffective : (rows: List a) -> (wireName: String) -> Maybe a
ttProjectedFindEffective rows wireName = case head rows of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just row -> if eq row.effectiveWire wireName then Just row else ttProjectedFindEffective (ssRest rows) wireName

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedAligned : (left: List a) -> (right: List b) -> Boolean
ttProjectedAligned left right = case head left of
  Nothing -> true
  Just row -> case ttProjectedFindKey right row.key of
    Nothing -> ttProjectedAligned (ssRest left) right
    Just other -> if ttProjectedRowAligned row other then ttProjectedAligned (ssRest left) right else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedRowAligned : (left: a) -> (right: b) -> Boolean
ttProjectedRowAligned left right =
  and (eq left.embeddedWire right.embeddedWire) (eq left.effectiveWire right.effectiveWire)

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedEmbeddedCollisionsSafe : (left: List a) -> (right: List b) -> Boolean
ttProjectedEmbeddedCollisionsSafe left right = case head left of
  Nothing -> true
  Just row -> case ttProjectedFindEmbedded right row.embeddedWire of
    Nothing -> ttProjectedEmbeddedCollisionsSafe (ssRest left) right
    Just other -> if fieldKeyEq row.key other.key then ttProjectedEmbeddedCollisionsSafe (ssRest left) right else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedEffectiveCollisionsSafe : (left: List a) -> (right: List b) -> Boolean
ttProjectedEffectiveCollisionsSafe left right = case head left of
  Nothing -> true
  Just row -> case ttProjectedFindEffective right row.effectiveWire of
    Nothing -> ttProjectedEffectiveCollisionsSafe (ssRest left) right
    Just other -> if fieldKeyEq row.key other.key then ttProjectedEffectiveCollisionsSafe (ssRest left) right else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttProjectedPairReady : (left: List a) -> (right: List b) -> Boolean
ttProjectedPairReady left right =
  if not (ttProjectedAligned left right) then false
  else if not (ttProjectedEmbeddedCollisionsSafe left right) then false
  else ttProjectedEffectiveCollisionsSafe left right

@category "engine-internal"
ttProductPairReady : (left: List a) -> (right: List b) -> (leftActive: String) -> (rightActive: String) -> Boolean
ttProductPairReady left right leftActive rightActive =
  if not (ttProductSingleReady left leftActive) then false
  else if not (ttProductSingleReady right rightActive) then false
  else ttProductPairProjectedReady left right

@category "engine-internal"
ttProductPairProjectedReady : (left: List a) -> (right: List b) -> Boolean
ttProductPairProjectedReady left right = case ttProjectSlots left of
  Nothing -> false
  Just leftRows -> case ttProjectSlots right of
    Nothing -> false
    Just rightRows -> ttProjectedPairReady leftRows rightRows

@category "engine-internal"
ttCaseNamesUnique : (cases: List a) -> Boolean
ttCaseNamesUnique cases = case head cases of
  Nothing -> true
  Just variantCase ->
    if ttCaseNameAppears (ssRest cases) variantCase.name
    then false
    else ttCaseNamesUnique (ssRest cases)

@category "engine-internal"
ttCaseNameAppears : (cases: List a) -> (name: String) -> Boolean
ttCaseNameAppears cases name = case findCaseByName cases name of
  Just _ -> true
  Nothing -> false

@category "engine-internal"
ttVariantActiveDiscriminator : (t: a) -> Maybe String
ttVariantActiveDiscriminator t = case ttExactMaybeInner t of
  Just _ -> Just ""
  Nothing -> ttOrdinaryVariantActiveDiscriminator t

@category "engine-internal"
ttOrdinaryVariantActiveDiscriminator : (t: a) -> Maybe String
ttOrdinaryVariantActiveDiscriminator t = case t of
  TtVariant { discriminator = discriminator } -> case discriminator of
    Nothing -> Just "$tag"
    Just name -> if eq name "$tag" then Just "$tag" else Nothing
  _ -> Nothing

@category "engine-internal"
ttCasePayloadsReady : (cases: List a) -> (active: String) -> Boolean
ttCasePayloadsReady cases active = case head cases of
  Nothing -> true
  Just variantCase ->
    if ttProductSingleReady variantCase.fields active
    then ttCasePayloadsReady (ssRest cases) active
    else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttVariantSingleReady : (t: a) -> Boolean
ttVariantSingleReady t = case ttVariantActiveDiscriminator t of
  Nothing -> false
  Just active -> ttVariantSingleReadyWith t active

@category "engine-internal"
ttVariantSingleReadyWith : (t: a) -> (active: String) -> Boolean
ttVariantSingleReadyWith t active =
  let cases = tsVariantCases t
  if ttCaseNamesUnique cases then ttCasePayloadsReady cases active else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttSharedCasePayloadsReady : (left: List a) -> (right: List b) -> (leftActive: String) -> (rightActive: String) -> Boolean
ttSharedCasePayloadsReady left right leftActive rightActive = case head left of
  Nothing -> true
  Just variantCase -> case findCaseByName right variantCase.name of
    Nothing -> ttSharedCasePayloadsReady (ssRest left) right leftActive rightActive
    Just other -> ttSharedPayloadStep variantCase other (ssRest left) right leftActive rightActive

@category "engine-internal"
ttSharedPayloadStep : (leftCase: a) -> (rightCase: b) -> (leftRest: List a) -> (right: List b) -> (leftActive: String) -> (rightActive: String) -> Boolean
ttSharedPayloadStep leftCase rightCase leftRest right leftActive rightActive =
  if ttProductPairReady leftCase.fields rightCase.fields leftActive rightActive
  then ttSharedCasePayloadsReady leftRest right leftActive rightActive
  else false

@category "engine-internal"
ttVariantPairReady : (left: a) -> (right: b) -> Boolean
ttVariantPairReady left right = case ttVariantActiveDiscriminator left of
  Nothing -> false
  Just leftActive -> case ttVariantActiveDiscriminator right of
    Nothing -> false
    Just rightActive -> ttVariantPairReadyWith left right leftActive rightActive

@category "engine-internal"
ttVariantPairReadyWith : (left: a) -> (right: b) -> (leftActive: String) -> (rightActive: String) -> Boolean
ttVariantPairReadyWith left right leftActive rightActive =
  if not (ttVariantSingleReadyWith left leftActive) then false
  else if not (ttVariantSingleReadyWith right rightActive) then false
  else ttSharedCasePayloadsReady (tsVariantCases left) (tsVariantCases right) leftActive rightActive

-- The terminal shape delegates to validationListInnerVariant.  Only wrapper
-- classification is new here.
@category "engine-internal"
ttListLegacyBarrier : (t: a) -> ContainmentListFace
ttListLegacyBarrier t = case peelListElem t of
  Just _ -> TtClBlocked
  Nothing -> TtClOther

@category "engine-internal"
ttListMuFace : (body: a) -> ContainmentListFace
ttListMuFace body = case body of
  TtVariant { cases = cases } -> case validationListInnerVariant cases of
    Just elem -> TtClLive { elem = elem }
    Nothing -> TtClBlocked
  _ -> TtClBlocked

@category "engine-internal"
ttListOpaqueVariantFace : (node: a) -> (cases: List b) -> ContainmentListFace
ttListOpaqueVariantFace node cases = case validationListInnerVariant cases of
  Just elem -> TtClLive { elem = elem }
  Nothing -> ttListLegacyBarrier node

-- Once an opaque prefix has been crossed, only validation's own primitive-name
-- boundary can prove that a named/refined leaf is not a hidden List.  Every
-- other name may be rebound by $defs, a registry, eval context, or the catalog.
@category "engine-internal"
ttListPostPrefixLeaf : (node: a) -> ContainmentListFace
ttListPostPrefixLeaf node = case node of
  TtRefined { base = base } -> ttListPostPrefixLeaf base
  TtNamed { name = name } -> if validationPrimitiveName name then TtClOther else TtClBlocked
  _ -> TtClBlocked

@category "engine-internal"
ttListOpaqueFace : (pure: a) -> ContainmentListFace
ttListOpaqueFace pure = case pure of
  TtOpaque { pure = nested } -> ttListOpaqueFace nested
  TtVariant { cases = cases } -> ttListOpaqueVariantFace pure cases
  TtMu { body = body } -> ttListMuFace body
  TtRefined { base = base } -> ttListPostPrefixLeaf base
  TtNamed {} -> ttListPostPrefixLeaf pure
  _ -> ttListLegacyBarrier pure

@category "engine-internal"
ttListFace : (t: a) -> ContainmentListFace
ttListFace t = case t of
  TtVariant {} -> TtClOther
  TtMu { body = body } -> ttListMuFace body
  TtOpaque { pure = pure } -> ttListOpaqueFace pure
  TtNamed {} -> TtClOther
  _ -> ttListLegacyBarrier t

@category "engine-internal"
ttListBypassKind : (kind: String) -> Boolean
ttListBypassKind kind =
  or (eq kind "union") (or (eq kind "intersect") (or (eq kind "complement") (eq kind "refined")))

-- disjointUnion — (A ∪ B) disjoint from `other` iff EVERY branch is disjoint
-- (mAnd-fold of the recursive disjoint over the marshalled branch operands). An
-- empty branch list ⇒ Just true (∪∅ = ∅). Sound AND complete.
@label "disjoint: disjointUnion"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b / floor-kernel Phase 3c / type-substrate P1(a.5) — a TraversalType union is disjoint from other iff every branch is; mAnd-fold the unified disjoint member. Commutativity serves a union on either side. THREADS `rp` rather than resetting it (round-3 review): when the union IS the `pure` view of a peeled `$opaque`, that opaque's representation still transports its branches, so a branch is NOT \"a written type in its own right\" and the carrier rules must stay refused. Propagating an already-set flag is strictly conservative — a top-level union arrives with rp already false. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointUnion : (rp: Boolean) -> (branches: List a) -> (other: b) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointUnion rp branches other = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just b -> mAnd (disjointW rp b other) (disjointUnion rp (ssRest branches) other)

-- disjointIntersectOp — (A ∩ B) disjoint from `other` if ANY branch is (A∩B ⊆ A,
-- so a disjoint branch proves the whole). Just true on a positive proof, else
-- Nothing (emTrueOnly drops each branch's Just false). Sound (not complete).
@label "disjoint: disjointIntersectOp"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b / type-substrate P1(a.5) — the intersect arm of disjoint: an intersect is disjoint from `other` if ANY branch is (A∩B ⊆ A). mOr-fold of emTrueOnly(disjointW rp branch other); Just true on a proof else Nothing. THREADS `rp` for the same reason disjointUnion does — an intersect that is a peeled `$opaque`'s pure view still rides that opaque's representation. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointIntersectOp : (rp: Boolean) -> (branches: List a) -> (other: b) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointIntersectOp rp branches other = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b -> mOr (emTrueOnly (disjointW rp b other)) (disjointIntersectOp rp (ssRest branches) other)

-- ── Phase 2.4 — the variant-vs-variant disjoint-by-tag arm ──────────────────
-- Two $variants reach disjointLeaf's same-shape arm (kind "$variant" both) and
-- coarsen to Nothing. But disjointness is decidable at the TAG level: distinct
-- constructor tags force it (no value carries a tag in both ⇒ ⟦Va⟧ ∩ ⟦Vb⟧ = ∅).
-- Ordinary variants retain the tag fold only after the P1(a.6) whole-variant
-- face gate. Exact Maybe is a forwarding carrier: exact/exact yields a
-- plan-ready overlap and mixed exact/ordinary pairs abstain.

-- bothVariant — the dispatch gate: fire disjointVariant ONLY when BOTH operands are
-- $variants (so every non-variant decision stays the byte-identical leaf cascade).
@label "disjoint: bothVariant"
@description "Phase 2.4 — the variant-arm gate of disjoint: true iff both operands are kind \"$variant\". Gates disjointVariant so a variant-vs-non-variant (or any other) pair falls to the unchanged disjointLeaf cascade (byte-identity preserved). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
bothVariant : (da: a) -> (db: b) -> Boolean
bothVariant da db = if eq (tsKind da) "variant" then eq (tsKind db) "variant" else false

-- disjointVariant — fold over da's cases, mAnd-ing each shared tag's product-
-- disjointness; a da-only tag contributes Just true (no value witnesses overlap on
-- a tag db lacks); no shared tag at all ⇒ Just true.
@label "disjoint: disjointVariant"
@description "Phase 2.4 / floor-kernel Phase 3c / type-substrate P1(a.6) — partition variant disjointness by the exact Maybe authority. Exact/exact returns plan-ready Just false because both accept null; an exact/ordinary pair abstains. Ordinary/ordinary first requires unique names, the live default discriminator, and complete keyed-product face gates, then folds shared-tag payload disjointness."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointVariant : (da: a) -> (db: b) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointVariant da db = case ttExactMaybeInner da of
  Just _ -> disjointVariantExactLeft da db
  Nothing -> disjointVariantOrdinaryLeft da db

@category "engine-internal"
disjointVariantExactLeft : (da: a) -> (db: b) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointVariantExactLeft da db = case ttExactMaybeInner db of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just _ ->
    if and (ttValidationPlanReady da) (ttValidationPlanReady db)
    then Just false
    else Nothing

@category "engine-internal"
disjointVariantOrdinaryLeft : (da: a) -> (db: b) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointVariantOrdinaryLeft da db = case ttExactMaybeInner db of
  Just _ -> Nothing
  Nothing ->
    if ttVariantPairReady da db
    then disjointVariantFold (tsVariantCases da) (tsVariantCases db)
    else Nothing

@label "disjoint: disjointVariantFold"
@description "Phase 2.4 / floor-kernel Phase 3c — mAnd-fold over the first variant's TtVariantCases; exhausted means every shared tag payload was disjoint (or no tag was shared). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointVariantFold : (acases: List a) -> (bcases: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointVariantFold acases bcases = case head acases of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just ac -> mAnd (disjointVariantOne ac bcases) (disjointVariantFold (ssRest acases) bcases)

@label "disjoint: disjointVariantOne"
@description "Phase 2.4 / floor-kernel Phase 3c / field-identity Phase 3 — one TtVariantCase's contribution: absent tag in the other case list ⇒ Just true; a shared tag delegates to FieldKey-aligned productDisjoint over the two validated TtField lists. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
disjointVariantOne : (acase: a) -> (bcases: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
disjointVariantOne acase bcases = case findCaseByName bcases (tsCaseName acase) of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just bcase -> productDisjoint (tsCaseFields acase) (tsCaseFields bcase)

-- productDisjoint — after both payloads pass the shared keyed-product face
-- fence, products are disjoint iff SOME aligned semantic factor is disjoint.
-- The fence checks embedded and scoped-effective coordinates independently,
-- widget occurrence policy, reserved wires, child plans, and pair alignment.
@label "disjoint: productDisjoint"
@description "Phase 2.4 / floor-kernel Phase 3c / type-substrate P1(a.6) — require both complete products to pass the embedded/effective-coordinate, plan, reserved-wire, and occurrence-policy fence. Then require equal arity and mOr-fold disjointness over semantic-FieldKey-aligned factors. Both empty yields Just false; every failed preflight/alignment yields Nothing."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
productDisjoint : (apay: List a) -> (bpay: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
productDisjoint apay bpay =
  if not (ttProductPairReady apay bpay "" "")
  then Nothing
  else if eq (length apay) (length bpay)
  then productDisjointByKey apay bpay
  else Nothing

@label "disjoint: productDisjointByKey"
@description "FieldKey-aligned product-disjoint fold after equal-arity and semantic-slot validation. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "disjoint" "field-identity" "phase-3"
@category "engine-internal"
productDisjointByKey : (apay: List a) -> (bpay: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
productDisjointByKey apay bpay = case head apay of
  Nothing -> Just false
  Just af ->
    case findFieldByKey bpay (tsFieldKey af) of
      Nothing -> Nothing
      Just bf -> mOr (disjoint (tsFieldType af) (tsFieldType bf)) (productDisjointByKey (ssRest apay) bpay)

-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- subset — ⟦have⟧ ⊆ ⟦want⟧ ?  (Tri = Just true | Just false | Nothing)
-- The containment relation's CORE member (Step 2). Folds the LIVE
-- `engine:typeSubsumes` (the editor's FunctionPicker ⊆-arm) into a SOUND
-- `subset` via a single PARAMETERIZED CORE `subsetW picker`, of which
-- `typeSubsumes` is the picker-view collapse and `subset` is the sound member.
-- North-star: design/types-are-sets-and-the-containment-substrate.md §4 + §6.
-- Step-0 probe verdict: notes/phase-6-step2-step0-probe.md.
--
-- ── Why a parameterized core, not a flat wrapper (probe §3) ──────────────────
-- C-2 Option A's "thin wrapper over subset" is idealized: TWO of the three
-- picker divergences live INSIDE the recursion, so a flat `Nothing → True`
-- post-collapse of a sound `subset` would REGRESS the picker:
--   (1) var-in-`want`         picker ⇒ Just true   ·  sound ⇒ Nothing (undecidable)
--   (2) refined-leaf Nothing  picker ⇒ base-congruence FALL-THROUGH (can still be
--                             `false`!) · sound ⇒ surface `decideSubset`'s Nothing
--   (3) composite formers     picker ⇒ constructor-level Just true · sound ⇒
--                             component-wise (Step 2b; coarse `Just true` in 2a)
-- So `subsetW` threads a `picker` flag; `subsetW True` reproduces the current
-- `typeSubsumes` arm-for-arm (oracle byte-green), `subsetW False` is the sound
-- `⊆`. ONE recursion, two views — C-2 Option A done right (NOT Option C's two
-- near-duplicate walks). The shared `ts*` accessors stay in type-subsumes.fenel
-- (same `module engine`), reused cross-file; the superseded `tsSameKind` /
-- `tsRefinedSubset` / `tsMaybeCongruent` are RETIRED there (subsumed by
-- `ssSameKind` / `ssRefined` / `ssMaybeCongruent`).
--
-- The refined-leaf delegation to `set:decideSubset` (resolved as bare
-- `decideSubset` via the existing decideSubsetSlice harness, eng-bodies-
-- dispatch.ts:178) is the structural→predicate seam (north-star §2), shared by
-- both views; the SOUND member surfaces its `Nothing` directly (C-1).
--
-- ── Recursive-type posture after type-substrate P1(a.6) ─────────────────────
-- Picker mode retains the legacy permissive μ/List shortcuts. Sound Tt mode no
-- longer claims generic μ congruence or that syntactic μX.X is a live-face
-- bottom: both abstain. The only recursive covariance retained here is an exact
-- LiveList pair under the validation List recognizer and complete plan/
-- occurrence readiness. The SetExpr Park rule remains the general μ judgment.
-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Subset (⊆) — parameterized core"
@description "set-algebra-to-fenel Phase 6 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — parameterized structural subset. Picker mode preserves the legacy permissive List peel, bottom-mu shortcut, refined fall-through, and constructor-level composite choices. Sound mode preserves Void, fences bottom/non-live mu, routes top-level Boolean/refined formers first, then classifies each operand as LiveList, FaceBlocked, or NotList; only two ready LiveLists recurse covariantly. Remaining sound forms dispatch through subsetWV and the gated same-kind rules."
@tags "engine" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "subtype" "phase-6"
subsetW : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetW picker have want =
  if tsIsVoid have then Just true
  else if isBottomMu have then if picker then Just true else Nothing
  else if picker then subsetWL picker have want
  else subsetWSoundPrelude have want

@label "subset: subsetWL"
@description "Phase 5 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — PICKER-only legacy List fast path, preserved textually: permissively peel both operands and recurse covariantly when both peel; otherwise fall through to subsetWV. Sound mode uses the separate exact three-outcome classifier."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetWL : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWL picker have want = case peelListElem have of
  Nothing -> subsetWV picker have want
  Just he -> subsetWLW picker he have want

@label "subset: subsetWLW"
@description "Phase 5 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — picker-only want-side of the preserved permissive List peel: with a peeled have element, recurse when want also peels; otherwise fall through to subsetWV."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetWLW : (picker: Boolean) -> (he: a) -> (have: b) -> (want: b) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWLW picker he have want = case peelListElem want of
  Nothing -> subsetWV picker have want
  Just we -> subsetW picker he we

@category "engine-internal"
subsetWSoundPrelude : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWSoundPrelude have want =
  let hk = tsKind have
  let wk = tsKind want
  if or (ttListBypassKind hk) (ttListBypassKind wk)
  then subsetWV false have want
  else subsetWSoundListFaces have want (ttListFace have) (ttListFace want)

@category "engine-internal"
subsetWSoundListFaces : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> (haveFace: ContainmentListFace) -> (wantFace: ContainmentListFace) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWSoundListFaces have want haveFace wantFace = case haveFace of
  TtClLive { elem = elem } -> subsetWSoundListLive have want elem wantFace
  TtClBlocked -> Nothing
  TtClOther -> subsetWSoundListOther have want wantFace

@category "engine-internal"
subsetWSoundListLive : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> (haveElem: b) -> (wantFace: ContainmentListFace) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWSoundListLive have want haveElem wantFace = case wantFace of
  TtClLive { elem = wantElem } ->
    if and (ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady have) (ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady want)
    then subsetW false haveElem wantElem
    else Nothing
  _ -> Nothing

@category "engine-internal"
subsetWSoundListOther : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> (wantFace: ContainmentListFace) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWSoundListOther have want wantFace = case wantFace of
  TtClOther -> subsetWV false have want
  _ -> Nothing

@label "subset: subsetWV"
@description "Phase 5 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — the var/kind tail after picker List peeling or sound List classification: a type-variable expected slot enters ssVarArm; otherwise dispatch by kind through subsetWK."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetWV : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWV picker have want =
  if tsIsVar want then ssVarArm picker have want
  else subsetWK picker have want (tsKind have) (tsKind want)

-- ── List recognizer (returns the MARSHALLED element type) ────────────────────
-- Mirrors set-algebra-deciders' peelList but returns the marshalled head TYPE
-- (for the subsetW recursion) rather than the raw head. Recognises the canonical
-- Nil/Cons spine through $refined / $opaque / $mu wrappers (both the Phase-2.5
-- $variant-self-ref pure form and the legacy μ form).
@label "subset: peelListElem"
@description "Phase 5 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — legacy permissive List-element peel retained for picker identity and classifier barrier detection. It crosses refined/opaque/mu wrappers and accepts a loose Nil/Cons structural shape by canonical head FieldKey. Sound LiveList recognition instead uses validationListInnerVariant's exact terminal grammar."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
peelListElem : (t: a) -> Maybe b
peelListElem t =
  if eq (tsKind t) "refined" then peelListElem (tsBase t)
  else if eq (tsKind t) "opaque" then peelListElem (tsPure t)
  else if eq (tsKind t) "mu" then peelListElem (tsMuBody t)
  else if eq (tsKind t) "variant" then peelListCons (tsVariantCases t)
  else Nothing

@label "subset: peelListCons"
@description "Phase 5 / field-identity Phase 3 — given a variant's case list, validate the Nil/Cons List shape and return the Cons payload field with the canonical List-head FieldKey. Else Nothing. Internal helper to peelListElem."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
peelListCons : (cs: List a) -> Maybe b
peelListCons cs = case findCaseByName cs "Cons" of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just consCase -> peelListConsHead cs consCase

@label "subset: peelListConsHead"
@description "Phase 5 / field-identity Phase 3 — having found the Cons case, require a sibling Nil case and return the canonical List-head FieldKey component's marshalled type. The recognizer consults neither current wire spelling nor declaration order. Internal helper to peelListCons."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
peelListConsHead : (cs: List a) -> (consCase: c) -> Maybe b
peelListConsHead cs consCase = case findCaseByName cs "Nil" of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just nilCase -> case findFieldByKey (tsCaseFields consCase) (canonicalListHeadFieldKey ()) of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just hf -> Just (tsFieldType hf)

@label "subset: isBottomMu"
@description "Phase 5 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — recognize the syntactic μX.X shortcut. Picker mode preserves its legacy Just true; sound mode returns Nothing because validation and matchesShape do not establish this syntax as a live-face bottom."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
isBottomMu : (t: a) -> Boolean
isBottomMu t = case t of
  TtMu { body = b } -> tsIsVar b
  _ -> false

@label "subset: ssVarArm"
@description "Phase 5 (E-void / E-var) — the want-is-var arm of subsetW: a same-named type-VAR on both sides ⇒ Just true (reflexivity — underpins $mu / List congruence where `tail:X ⊆ X`); else the generous/undecidable ssVar split. (The ∅ ⊆ anything void short-circuit precedes this in subsetW, so `void ⊆ var` is still Just true.) Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
ssVarArm : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssVarArm picker have want =
  if tsSameVar have want then Just true else ssVar picker

@label "subset: tsSameVar"
@description "Phase 5 (E-var) — are both operands the SAME type-variable (TtVar with equal names)? Internal helper to ssVarArm."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
tsSameVar : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Boolean
tsSameVar have want = if tsIsVar have then eq (tsVarName have) (tsVarName want) else false

@label "subset: tsVarName"
@description "Phase 5 (E-var) — the name of a TtVar (else empty). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
tsVarName : (t: a) -> String
tsVarName t = case t of
  TtVar { name = n } -> n
  _ -> ""

@label "subset: ssVar"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 — the type-variable expected-slot arm of subsetW: picker mode accepts ANY have (Just true, the polymorphic-slot accept); SOUND mode ⇒ Nothing (a free type-var's denotation is unknown ⇒ undecidable). Internal helper to subsetW."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssVar : (picker: Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
ssVar picker = if picker then Just true else Nothing

@label "subset: ssKinds"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 / type-substrate P1(a.5)+P1(a.6) — kind dispatch after the var/List prelude. Boolean formers route first; refined and opaque handling lives below; equal residual kinds enter ssSameKind; a genuine unresolved kind mismatch reaches ttSubsetSortRefute, which currently abstains unconditionally."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetWK : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> (hk: String) -> (wk: String) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWK picker have want hk wk =
  -- containment-substrate Phase 2 Step 1b — the tier-2 former arms (checked FIRST,
  -- before refined/opaque stripping, so a former on either side dispatches to its
  -- own combinator). All sound MODULO THE LEDGER'S OPEN ROWS — `t.top.opaque` is
  -- a SIDE-CONDITIONED row (round 10: no executed refutation; entitled while an
  -- opaque's live faces implement its `pure` view) reached from the LHS-complement
  -- arm below, and `t.sub.resolve` is MISSING rather than wrong — so read "sound"
  -- as "sound where `design/tcb-ledger.md` does not say otherwise":
  -- LHS union ⇒ ∀ branch ⊆ want (mAnd); RHS union ⇒
  -- ∃ branch (Just true if any, else Nothing); LHS intersect ⇒ ∃ branch ⊆ want;
  -- RHS intersect ⇒ ∀ branch (mAnd); RHS complement ⇒ disjoint have inner; LHS
  -- complement ⇒ picker stays generous; sound mode asks the exact Tt top-cover
  -- presentation of ¬A⊆B iff A∪B=top. The leaf cascade
  -- (refined/opaque/same-kind) stays in subsetWKBase — a separate fn so this
  -- chain is single-line throughout (the Fenel-bodied parser fences a multiline
  -- `then`/`else` MIXED into a single-line else-if chain).
  if eq hk "union" then subsetUnionHave picker (tsUnionBranches have) want
  else if eq hk "intersect" then subsetIntersectHave picker (tsIntersectBranches have) want
  else if eq hk "complement" then ttSubsetComplement picker have want
  else if eq wk "union" then subsetUnionWant picker have (tsUnionBranches want)
  else if eq wk "intersect" then subsetIntersectWant picker have (tsIntersectBranches want)
  else if eq wk "complement" then ttDisjoint have (tsComplementInner want)
  else subsetWKBase picker have want hk wk

@label "subset: ttSubsetComplement"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — LHS TtComplement subset: picker mode preserves its generous Just true; sound mode decides ¬A⊆B through the shared Tt top-equivalence presentation topCover(nnf(A∪B)). Outside the exact structural pairing slice it remains Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "complement" "top-cover" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttSubsetComplement : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ttSubsetComplement picker have want =
  if picker then Just true
  else
    let inner = tsComplementInner have
    let branches = appendItem want (appendItem inner [])
    let joined = TtUnion { branches = branches, raw = have }
    ttTopCover (ttNnf joined)

@label "subset: ssKindsBase"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 / Phase 2 Step 1b / type-substrate P1(a.5) — the leaf-cascade tail of subsetWK (after the tier-2 former arms): refined/refined ⇒ ssRefined; mixed refined ⇒ strip + recurse; opaque layers transparent; same non-refined/non-opaque kind ⇒ ssSameKind; kind mismatch ⇒ the ttSubsetSortRefute tail, not a blanket Just false. Split out so subsetWK's tier-2 chain stays single-line. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetWKBase : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> (hk: String) -> (wk: String) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWKBase picker have want hk wk =
  if eq hk "refined" then ssRefinedHave picker have want
  else if eq wk "refined" then ssBRefined picker have want
  else subsetWKLeaf picker have want hk wk

@label "subset: ssRefinedHave"
@description "Phase 5 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — picker preserves the legacy opaque-reveal/base-forget expression. Sound mode first requires complete plan and occurrence readiness; a revealed refined want uses the positive-only two-coordinate rule, while base-forget keeps only a recursive Just true and drops every negative/unknown."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
ssRefinedHave : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssRefinedHave picker have want =
  if picker
  then case peelToRefined want of
    Just wref -> ssRefined picker have wref
    Nothing -> subsetW picker (tsBase have) want
  else ssRefinedHaveSound have want

@category "engine-internal"
ssRefinedHaveSound : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssRefinedHaveSound have want =
  if not (and (ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady have) (ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady want))
  then Nothing
  else case peelToRefined want of
    Just wref -> ssRefinedCoordinates have wref
    Nothing -> ttKeepTrue (subsetW false (tsBase have) want)

@label "subset: peelToRefined"
@description "Phase 5 — peel a type through its opaque layers to a refined form: TtRefined ⇒ Just it; TtOpaque ⇒ recurse its pure view; else Nothing. The `while opaque bp = bp.pure` copy-peel isSubtype's refined-a arm does to test whether b reveals a refinement. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
peelToRefined : (t: a) -> Maybe a
peelToRefined t =
  if eq (tsKind t) "refined" then Just t
  else if eq (tsKind t) "opaque" then peelToRefined (tsPure t)
  else Nothing

@label "subset: ssKindsLeaf"
@description "Phase 5 / type-substrate P1(a.5) — the leaf tail of subsetWKBase (split for the per-decl token cap): the named/opaque nominal-name bridge (ssNominalBridge ⇒ Just true) FIRST, then the opaque peels (have/want), then same-kind congruence (ssSameKind), else the kind-mismatch tail ssResolve (which refutes only on a proven host-carrier partition; it no longer refutes on kind difference alone). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetWKLeaf : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> (hk: String) -> (wk: String) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetWKLeaf picker have want hk wk =
  if ssNominalBridge have want then Just true
  else if eq hk "opaque" then subsetW picker (tsPure have) want
  else if eq wk "opaque" then subsetW picker have (tsPure want)
  else if eq hk wk then ssSameKind picker hk have want
  else ssResolve picker have want hk wk

-- ── Phase 5 (R-resolve) — ref resolution + co-induction (fully in Fenel) ─────
-- A TtNamed leaf NOT decided by the nominal-name arm (a registry alias whose
-- referent is structural, e.g. {$ref:"RecordAlias"} ⊆ a $record) resolves via the
-- `resolveRef` ctx-native (the global universal registry read, getEntityTypeByName
-- → marshalled Tt*) and recurses on the referent (isSubtype's arm-2 resolve-then-
-- recurse, now in Fenel). A `seen` memo (List of {h,w} marshalled-type pairs)
-- threads through the resolve chain ONLY (the structural tree is finite); at re-
-- entry of a pair already on the stack ⇒ Just true (the co-inductive accept, for
-- cyclic entities like SelfRef := {$ref:"SelfRef"}). PICKER mode does NOT resolve
-- (kept byte-identical — a kind mismatch stays Just false).

@label "subset: ssResolve"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) / type-substrate P1(a.5) — the kind-mismatch tail of subsetWKLeaf: picker mode ⇒ Just false (byte-identical; the picker does not resolve refs). The SUBSET half of the P1(a.5) repair is entirely below this split, but the DISJOINT half is NOT unreachable from picker mode — `subsetWK`'s want-side complement arm calls `ttDisjoint` with no picker flag. The picker is nevertheless unmoved because every cell that repair changed went `Just true` → `Nothing`, and typeSubsumes collapses `Nothing → true`; that is pinned, not assumed (type-substrate-p1a5-tt-object-carrier.test.ts, \"the ONE un-picker-gated route into disjoint\"). SOUND mode ⇒ resolveArm (resolve whichever side is a TtNamed registry alias and recurse on the referent, with a co-induction memo seeded empty; a genuine mismatch then reaches the ttSubsetSortRefute fence). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
ssResolve : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> (hk: String) -> (wk: String) -> Maybe Boolean
ssResolve picker have want hk wk =
  if picker then Just false else resolveArm [] have want hk wk

@label "subset: resolveArm"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) / type-substrate P1(a.5) — sound named resolution: resolve a named have or want through resolveRef with the co-induction memo; if neither side is named, enter ttSubsetSortRefute, whose current implementation abstains unconditionally. The blanket different-kind refutation is retired."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
resolveArm : (seen: List p) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> (hk: String) -> (wk: String) -> Maybe Boolean
resolveArm seen have want hk wk =
  if eq hk "named" then resolveHaveSide seen have want
  else if eq wk "named" then resolveWantSide seen have want
  else ttSubsetSortRefute have hk wk

-- ── type-substrate P1(a.5) — the subset twin: the terminal never refutes ────
-- `have ⊆ want` is refuted iff SOME value of `have` is outside `want`. The old
-- terminal read "the kinds differ, so refute", which is the same producer claim
-- disjointLeaf carried, PLUS a second unstated premise: that `have` is inhabited.
-- BOTH are false, and the terminal now abstains unconditionally. Three separate
-- blockers, each MEASURED, and a future restoration must clear ALL of them:
--
--   (1) MOST KINDS ARE NOT SORTS. This terminal is reached by FAR more than the
--       six rigid kinds — `mu`, `var`, `app`, `el`, `tagged`, `other` and
--       `unknown` all land here on a kind mismatch, and every one was REFUTED:
--         {$var:"a"} ⊆ record{}              instantiate a := record{} (or $void)
--         μX.(variant P{}) ⊆ record{}        {$tag:"P"} inhabits the open record
--         $tagged{value=record{}} ⊆ record{} the value-erasure reading
--
--   (2) ∅ ⊆ EVERYTHING. `subsetW`'s only emptiness short-circuits are SYNTACTIC
--       (`$void`, `μX.X`), so `record{x:$void}` — provably uninhabited — refuted
--       against a tuple. Any restored refutation must gate on the file's own
--       SOUND `empty` decider returning `Just false` (decidably NONempty), and
--       must NOT collapse it through `emptyB`, which maps undecided to false and
--       would read "undecided" as "known inhabited".
--
--   (3) THE PEEL, which is why this is a FENCE and not a narrowed rule. Unlike
--       `disjointW`, the subset walk has no `rp` flag: `subsetWKLeaf` peels
--       `$opaque` by re-entering `subsetW`, and `$opaque` is exactly the wrapper
--       that swaps the runtime carrier for the pure ADT. `Int` peels to `$record`
--       while holding NUMBERS, `List` peels to `$variant` while holding ARRAYS.
--       So at this terminal the kind pair describes the PURE views and the
--       carrier partition it would cite is unavailable. Threading the flag here
--       means an extra parameter on nine functions (subsetW → subsetWL →
--       subsetWLW → subsetWV → subsetWK → subsetWKBase → subsetWKLeaf →
--       ssResolve → resolveArm) plus every call site — and it buys NOTHING
--       OBSERVABLE, because no consumer distinguishes `Just false` from
--       `Nothing` on this path: `isSubtype` is `isJustTrue`, `conformCongruent`
--       is a Kleene `mAnd`, and the picker exits above the split. Priced, named,
--       and deliberately not built.
@label "subset: ttSubsetSortRefute"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.5) — the cross-kind subset terminal, which ABSTAINS unconditionally. Retained as the named anchor for TCB row t.sub.kind-mismatch and for any future restoration, which must clear three measured blockers: most kinds reaching here are not host sorts at all (mu/var/app/el/tagged/other/unknown were all being refuted); the empty set is a subset of everything and subsetW's only emptiness short-circuits are syntactic; and the subset walk peels `$opaque` without tracking it, so the kind pair at this point describes the pure ADT views rather than the runtime carriers (Int peels to $record but holds numbers; List peels to $variant but holds arrays). The disjoint face keeps its carrier rules because disjointW threads that peel flag. No consumer distinguishes Just false from Nothing here. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "type-substrate" "phase-1a5"
@category "engine-internal"
ttSubsetSortRefute : (have: a) -> (hk: String) -> (wk: String) -> Maybe Boolean
ttSubsetSortRefute have hk wk = Nothing

@label "subset: resolveHaveSide"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) — resolve the have-side TtNamed: the co-inductive accept (this (have,want) pair already on the resolve stack ⇒ Just true), else resolve the name and recurse with the pair pushed. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
resolveHaveSide : (seen: List p) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
resolveHaveSide seen have want =
  if seenPair seen have want then Just true
  else resolveHaveStep (appendItem (mkPair have want) seen) have want

@label "subset: resolveHaveStep"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) / type-substrate P1(a.8) — resolve the have name via the resolveRef ctx-native: Nothing (unresolvable) ⇒ NOTHING; Just referent ⇒ reenterHave on the marshalled referent. The old `Just false` was the CLOSED-WORLD refutation and is RETIRED as a false definite (`t.sub.resolve` condition 2). Ground, and it needed no owner ruling: `Just false` asserts ∃v ∈ ⟦have⟧ ∖ ⟦want⟧. Under an OPEN world ⟦unresolvable⟧ is unknown, so no definite follows; under a CLOSED world the name is ill-formed and has no denotation, so again no definite follows. NEITHER documented reading entitles the refutation — standing rule C, design/deciding.md §9.1. MEASURED at entry: `sub({$ref:<unregistered>}, $void)` = `Just false`, and it was the most definite composite path left after P1(a.7) fenced its siblings. ⚠ SEPARATE, UNREPAIRED, and the reason `t.sub.resolve` lands MISSING rather than SIDE-CONDITIONED: the SUCCESS path is unreachable at HEAD. The native marshals the identified referent and then hands that already-marshalled value to a helper that marshals it AGAIN (engine-bodies-dispatch.ts:11345 → :9152), so the own-data boundary rejects it and EVERY resolvable name degrades to a miss — MEASURED `sub({$ref:\"Bot\"}, record{})` = `Just false` while `getIdentifiedEntityTypeByName(\"Bot\")` returns a type. Repairing that is NOT a monotone rider (it reactivates definite successes and exposes the fresh-memo cycle question), so it is filed, not fixed here. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
resolveHaveStep : (seen: List p) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
resolveHaveStep seen have want = case resolveRef (tsName have) of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just r -> reenterHave seen r want

@label "subset: reenterHave"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) — after resolving the have side: a referent that is ITSELF a TtNamed (a self/chain ref) re-enters resolveHaveSide WITH the accumulated seen (so a cycle is caught); a structural referent recurses the finite subsetW (sound mode, fresh memo — the structural tree terminates on its own). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
reenterHave : (seen: List p) -> (resolved: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
reenterHave seen resolved want =
  if eq (tsKind resolved) "named" then resolveHaveSide seen resolved want
  else subsetW false resolved want

@label "subset: resolveWantSide"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) — resolve the want-side TtNamed (the symmetric twin of resolveHaveSide): co-inductive accept on a repeated pair, else resolve + recurse with the pair pushed. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
resolveWantSide : (seen: List p) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
resolveWantSide seen have want =
  if seenPair seen have want then Just true
  else resolveWantStep (appendItem (mkPair have want) seen) have want

@label "subset: resolveWantStep"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) / type-substrate P1(a.8) — resolve the want name via resolveRef: Nothing ⇒ NOTHING; Just referent ⇒ reenterWant. The SEPARATELY REACHABLE twin of `resolveHaveStep`'s retirement (the have side is structural whenever this fires), retired on the same ground and carrying the same unrepaired success-path note. `t.sub.resolve` condition 2. MEASURED at entry: `sub(record{}, {$ref:<unregistered>})` = `Just false`. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
resolveWantStep : (seen: List p) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
resolveWantStep seen have want = case resolveRef (tsName want) of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just r -> reenterWant seen have r

@label "subset: reenterWant"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) — after resolving the want side: a still-named referent re-enters resolveWantSide with seen (cycle guard); a structural referent recurses the finite subsetW. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
reenterWant : (seen: List p) -> (have: a) -> (resolved: a) -> Maybe Boolean
reenterWant seen have resolved =
  if eq (tsKind resolved) "named" then resolveWantSide seen have resolved
  else subsetW false have resolved

@label "subset: mkPair"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) — a co-induction memo entry: the (have, want) marshalled-type pair pushed onto the resolve stack. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
mkPair : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> p
mkPair have want = { h = have, w = want }

@label "subset: seenPair"
@description "Phase 5 (R-resolve) — is the (have, want) pair already on the resolve stack? Structural deep-equality (deepEqValue) of both components against each memo entry — the co-inductive accept that makes cyclic-entity subtyping decidable. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
seenPair : (seen: List p) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Boolean
seenPair seen have want = case head seen of
  Nothing -> false
  Just p -> if and (deepEqValue p.h have) (deepEqValue p.w want) then true else seenPair (ssRest seen) have want

@label "subset: nominalNameOf"
@description "Phase 5 (E-named) — the nominal entity NAME of a leaf marshalled type as Maybe String: TtNamed ⇒ Just its name; TtOpaque ⇒ Just its `$opaque.name` (Char/Nat/Int/…). Else Nothing (a structural type has no single nominal name). Reproduces isSubtype's name-handle + opaque-name reads (the `$named↔$opaque` bridge + the named hierarchy). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
nominalNameOf : (t: a) -> Maybe String
nominalNameOf t = case t of
  TtNamed { name = n } -> Just n
  TtOpaque { name = n } -> Just n
  _ -> Nothing

@label "subset: ssNominalBridge"
@description "Phase 5 (E-named) — the named/opaque hierarchy bridge of subsetWKBase: when BOTH operands yield a nominal name (TtNamed or TtOpaque), is have's name a Subsumable subset of want's (namedSubsetCheck)? Reproduces isSubtype's `$named↔$named` hierarchy (Nat ⊆ Int) AND the `$named↔$opaque` bridge ({$named:\"Nat\"} ⊆ Nat-opaque). A POSITIVE-only gate: true ⇒ the caller short-circuits Just true; false ⇒ FALL THROUGH to the opaque peel (so Char-opaque ⊆ Nat-opaque, NOT a hierarchy fact, still decides via Char.pure's refinement-forget). Checked AFTER the refined arms, BEFORE the opaque peels. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
ssNominalBridge : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Boolean
ssNominalBridge have want =
  if isTtNamed have then bridgeNames have want
  else if isTtNamed want then bridgeNames have want
  else false

@label "subset: isTtNamed"
@description "Phase 5 (E-named) — is the leaf a bare name-handle (TtNamed, NOT an opaque)? Gates ssNominalBridge so it fires ONLY when ≥1 side is a name-handle — reproducing isSubtype's `$named↔$named` hierarchy + `$named↔$opaque` bridge WITHOUT short-circuiting opaque↔opaque (where the name alone is insufficient — `List Int ⊄ List Nat` despite both being the opaque `List`; those must PEEL to their pure form and compare element-wise). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
isTtNamed : (t: a) -> Boolean
isTtNamed t = eq (tsKind t) "named"

@label "subset: bridgeNames"
@description "Phase 5 (E-named) — both sides yield a nominal name (TtNamed or TtOpaque) ⇒ is have's name a Subsumable subset of want's (namedSubsetCheck)? The positive-only bridge body (gated by ssNominalBridge's ≥1-TtNamed check). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
bridgeNames : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Boolean
bridgeNames have want = case nominalNameOf have of
  Nothing -> false
  Just na ->
    case nominalNameOf want of
      Nothing -> false
      Just nb -> namedSubsetCheck na nb

@label "subset: ssBRefined"
@description "Phase 5 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — have-not-refined/want-refined. Picker keeps the legacy predicate-forgetting recursion. Sound mode requires both complete operands to be plan/occurrence ready, then preserves the existing rule: a provably top predicate compares against the base; otherwise only a conservative base refutation survives."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
ssBRefined : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssBRefined picker have want =
  if picker then subsetW true have (tsBase want)
  else if and (ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady have) (ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady want)
  then ssBRefinedSound have want
  else Nothing

@category "engine-internal"
ssBRefinedSound : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssBRefinedSound have want = case decideSubset SeAll (tsRefinedSet want) of
    Just true -> subsetW false have (tsBase want)
    _ -> containmentConservative (subsetW false have (tsBase want))

@label "subset: ssRefined"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — picker retains the legacy predicate decision and base fallback. Sound refined/refined requires complete plan/occurrence readiness and returns Just true only when both baseHave subset baseWant and setHave subset setWant are explicitly Just true; every false or unknown coordinate becomes Nothing."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssRefined : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssRefined picker have want =
  if picker
  then case decideSubset (tsRefinedSet have) (tsRefinedSet want) of
    Just b -> Just b
    Nothing -> subsetW picker (tsBase have) (tsBase want)
  else if and (ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady have) (ttOccurrenceConstraintsReady want)
    then ssRefinedCoordinates have want
    else Nothing

@category "engine-internal"
ssRefinedCoordinates : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssRefinedCoordinates have want = case subsetW false (tsBase have) (tsBase want) of
  Just true -> ttKeepTrue (decideSubset (tsRefinedSet have) (tsRefinedSet want))
  _ -> Nothing

@label "subset: ssSameKind"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — same-kind dispatch after former/refined/opaque routing. Named uses the picker/sound nominal split; variant uses the exact-Maybe/ordinary gate; generic mu recurses only in picker mode and abstains in sound mode; tagged recurses through its value carrier ONLY in picker mode and abstains in sound mode (P1(a.8), `t.sub.tagged`); record/arrow/map/tuple enter their picker or component-wise sound arms."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssSameKind : (picker: Boolean) -> (k: String) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssSameKind picker k have want =
  if eq k "named" then ssNamedArm picker (tsName have) (tsName want)
  else if eq k "variant" then ssVariant picker have want
  else if eq k "mu" then if picker then subsetW picker (tsMuBody have) (tsMuBody want) else Nothing
  else if eq k "tagged" then ssTagged picker have want
  else ssSameKindTail picker k have want

@label "subset: ssTagged"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.8) — the `$tagged` arm of ssSameKind, split on the picker flag. PICKER mode is BYTE-IDENTICAL (it recurses through the value carrier exactly as before). SOUND mode emits NOTHING in both polarities. Ground — standing rule C, reading-invariance (design/deciding.md §9.1): the two live faces disagree about what a `$tagged` DENOTES. Validation elaborates every `$tagged` to `VtTagged` and checks UUID SYNTAX ONLY, never reading the value slot (validate.fenel:899, :1240, :1548), while `matchesShape` recurses INTO that slot (decompose.fenel:77). Under the erasure reading every `$tagged` type has the SAME population — the UUID strings — so a refutation between two of them is false; under the recursion reading the wrapper is transparent and the value verdict lifts. A definite whose truth depends on which reading you pick is not entitled. MEASURED contradiction at entry: `validate($tagged{value=$void}, <uuid>)` and `validate($tagged{value=record{_0:Number}}, <uuid>)` are BOTH VALID while this arm returned `Just false` between them, and the emptiness twin called the first EMPTY. A phantom-EQUALITY gate was measured OUT — every contradiction cell already has EQUAL phantoms. Priced: tagged reflexivity, the brand positive (`Id<Bot> ⊆ Id<User>` was `Just true`), and the record-width refutation; recovery rides the `sub.refl.deepeq` slice plus the deferred brand ruling. Ledger `t.sub.tagged`. Internal helper to ssSameKind."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "tagged" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
ssTagged : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssTagged picker have want =
  if picker then subsetW picker (tsTaggedValue have) (tsTaggedValue want)
  else Nothing

@label "subset: ssNamedArm"
@description "decide-substrate (Tt* named-leaf honesty) / type-substrate P1(a.6) — the named-leaf arm of ssSameKind, split on the picker flag. PICKER mode is BYTE-IDENTICAL (Just (namedSubsetCheck na nb) — the UX list-membership: a refutation means 'not in the picker', not a truth claim). SOUND mode is POSITIVE-ONLY: forward namedSubsetCheck na nb ⇒ Just true; else Nothing. P1(a.6) RETIRED the reversed-proper Just false: its own worked example was Number ⊆ Int, and the live faces do not implement that distinction — validationValidateNamed sends Number/Int/Nat to ONE validationValidateNumber (validate.fenel:1250-1251) which rejects only NaN, so 1.5 and -1 validate as Nat, and matchesShape's named leaf is accept-all (decompose.fenel:60). The three names denote ONE population at both live faces, so the refutation was a false definite; witnesses 1.5 / [1.5] lift it through List covariance and every gate-ready product. Among validationPrimitiveName names the reversed-proper pairs are EXACTLY the numeric triple, so no sound negative is lost. Nonprimitive names abstain too: an unresolved name refuses every value (validate.fenel:1258), making ⟦have⟧ = ∅ and the negative vacuously false, and resolved population is caller-registry-scoped while this judgment carries no validation-source context. This makes the Tt named arm shape-identical to its already-positive-only SetExpr sibling. Re-introducing a negative requires a live-face SEPARATION witness, not a hierarchy fact; the named-arm honesty pins enforce that. Internal helper to ssSameKind."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssNamedArm : (picker: Boolean) -> (na: String) -> (nb: String) -> Maybe Boolean
ssNamedArm picker na nb =
  if picker then Just (namedSubsetCheck na nb)
  else if namedSubsetCheck na nb then Just true
  else Nothing

@label "subset: ssSameKindTail"
@description "Phase 5 — the unit/app/composite tail of ssSameKind (split for the per-decl token cap): unit ⇒ Just true (E-unit); app ⇒ ssApp (E-app); else the composite-former arm (record/arrow/map/tuple). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
ssSameKindTail : (picker: Boolean) -> (k: String) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssSameKindTail picker k have want =
  if eq k "unit" then Just true
  else if eq k "app" then ssApp picker have want
  else ssComposite picker k have want

@label "subset: ssApp"
@description "Phase 5 (E-app) / type-substrate P1(a.7) — the applied-type ($el.call ⇒ TtApp) arm of ssSameKind, split on the picker flag. PICKER mode is BYTE-IDENTICAL (same head ⇒ the pairwise args fold, else Just false — a presentation filter, not a truth claim). SOUND mode ABSTAINS in both polarities. TtApp.head is an ARBITRARY type-level function name, not a fixed ADT constructor, so `same head ⇒ covariant args` is an unchecked monotonicity premise over an OPEN head domain: a head whose result is antitone in its argument (anything producing `(a) -> Bool`, or a typeclass record such as `Eq a = Eq eq: a -> a -> Maybe Bool`) makes the positive conceptually FALSE, and neither live face can refute it because an unresolved VtEl accepts every value (validate.fenel:1551-1552) and matchesShape has no TtApp arm (decompose.fenel:82, `_ -> true`). The head-mismatch negative rides that same one-population fact. App reflexivity is a priced loss recoverable only by the deep-equality reflexivity twin. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
ssApp : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssApp picker have want =
  if not picker then Nothing
  else if eq (tsAppHead have) (tsAppHead want) then tupleSub picker (tsAppArgs have) (tsAppArgs want)
  else Just false

@label "subset: tsAppHead"
@description "Phase 5 (E-app) — the constructor head name of a TtApp (else empty). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
tsAppHead : (t: a) -> String
tsAppHead t = case t of
  TtApp { head = h } -> h
  _ -> ""

@label "subset: tsAppArgs"
@description "Phase 5 (E-app) — the arg-type list of a TtApp (else []). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
tsAppArgs : (t: a) -> List b
tsAppArgs t = case t of
  TtApp { args = as } -> as
  _ -> []

@label "subset: ssVariant"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — picker preserves the legacy Maybe-shaped congruence/constructor accept expression. Sound mode uses exact typeTraversalMaybeInner on both operands: exact/exact keeps only positive inner congruence after the full gate; exact-have/ordinary-want may emit the plan-ready null refutation; ordinary-have/exact-want abstains; ordinary/ordinary uses the unique/default-discriminator keyed-payload gate before variantSub."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssVariant : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssVariant picker have want =
  if picker then ssVariantPicker picker have want else ssVariantSound have want

@category "engine-internal"
ssVariantPicker : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssVariantPicker picker have want =
  if tsBothMaybe have want then ssMaybeCongruent picker have want
  else if picker then Just true
  else variantSub picker (tsVariantCases have) (tsVariantCases want)

@category "engine-internal"
ssVariantSound : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssVariantSound have want = case ttExactMaybeInner have of
  Just _ -> ssVariantSoundExactHave have want
  Nothing -> ssVariantSoundOrdinaryHave have want

@category "engine-internal"
ssVariantSoundExactHave : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssVariantSoundExactHave have want = case ttExactMaybeInner want of
  Just _ ->
    if ttVariantPairReady have want
    then ssMaybeCongruent false have want
    else Nothing
  -- Exact Maybe always admits null; an ordinary Variant never does.  This
  -- refutation depends on that carrier fact, not on the ordinary discriminator.
  Nothing -> if ttValidationPlanReady have then Just false else Nothing

@category "engine-internal"
ssVariantSoundOrdinaryHave : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssVariantSoundOrdinaryHave have want = case ttExactMaybeInner want of
  Just _ -> Nothing
  Nothing ->
    if ttVariantPairReady have want
    then variantSub false (tsVariantCases have) (tsVariantCases want)
    else Nothing

@label "subset: ssComposite"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 — the composite-former arm of ssSameKind (record / arrow / map / tuple): picker mode returns constructor-level Just true (ssCompositePicker, byte-preserved from 2a); SOUND mode (Step 2b) is component-wise (ssCompositeSound — record width+depth, arrow variance, tuple pairwise, map value-subset). Internal helper to ssSameKind."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssComposite : (picker: Boolean) -> (k: String) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssComposite picker k have want =
  if picker then ssCompositePicker k
  else ssCompositeSound picker k have want

@label "subset: ssCompositePicker"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 — the PICKER-mode composite arm (FROZEN, byte-identical to the 2a behaviour the FunctionPicker oracle pins): record / arrow / map / tuple match at constructor level (Just true); anything else ⇒ Just false. Internal helper to ssComposite."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssCompositePicker : (k: String) -> Maybe Boolean
ssCompositePicker k =
  if eq k "record" then Just true
  else if eq k "arrow" then Just true
  else if eq k "map" then Just true
  else if eq k "tuple" then Just true
  else Just false

-- ── type-substrate P1(a.7) — the top-level composite closure ────────────────
-- This arm is the LAST entry point that emitted structural definites with no
-- readiness gate at all (`t.sub.composite-toplevel-ungated`, UNSOUND-KNOWN).
-- The repair is PER-FORMER polarity surgery, not a uniform gate: a
-- `ttValidationPlanReady` consult here would be UNEXERCISABLE, because that
-- predicate answers `false` UNCONDITIONALLY for `TtArrow`, `TtMap` and (via the
-- tail) `TtTuple` — an always-false branch in the TCB is untestable code, not a
-- fence.  Per former:
--
--   record  unchanged.  `recordSubGated` already carries the complete
--           coordinate/occurrence fence AND the have-emptiness vacuity rescue.
--   tuple   POSITIVES ONLY (`ttKeepTrue`).  Two independent reasons, and the
--           first is a MEASURED false definite: `tupleSub`'s arity and slot
--           refutations have NO have-nonemptiness gate, unlike every sibling
--           product former (`recordSubGated`'s `anyEmpty` rescue,
--           `variantCaseSub`'s inhabitance gate, `arrowSub`'s `nonemptyKnown`),
--           so `tuple[Void, Number] ⊆ tuple[Void]` returned `Just false` while
--           ⟦have⟧ = ∅ at the conceptual reading AND at the implemented
--           `decomposeMatchesTuple` face.  Separately, the ITEM axis bottoms out
--           in `matchesShape`'s accept-all named leaf and validation's
--           `TtTuple → VtOther` refuse-all degrade, so no item separation is
--           entitled either.  The wrap is HERE and not inside `tupleSub`,
--           because PICKER-mode `ssApp` calls `tupleSub` on its args and must
--           stay byte-identical.  Recovery (out of phase): a have-nonemptiness-
--           gated arity rule — `decomposeMatchesTuple` really does implement the
--           arity axis, so that negative is recoverable with its own row.
--   arrow   NOTHING, both polarities.  Two independent IMPLEMENTED refuters
--           survive every arrow verdict: validation's registered-name
--           `paramCount` (validate.fenel:1528 — `"std:negate"` validates against
--           a 1-param have and is refused against a 2-param want, while
--           `arrowSub`'s `someParamEmptyW` short-circuit calls that pair
--           `Just true`), and the flatten/written-count divergence
--           (`ttArrowFlatten` curry-normalizes while validation counts the
--           UNFLATTENED `VtArrow` field list, validate.fenel:907-911).  The
--           `signatureSubtype` column is EXCLUDED as circular: it IS this
--           judgment.
--   map     NOTHING, both polarities.  `ssMap` reads `$map` as a partial
--           dictionary (`K1 ⊆ K2`) while `validationValidateMap`'s finite arm
--           requires a TOTAL array of length `card`, so `Map[3,T] ⊆ Map[4,T]`
--           was a false POSITIVE at an implemented arm and `ttKeepTrue` would
--           have retained it.  A key-EQUALITY-gated positive (the `conformMap`
--           rule) is reading-invariant and is the named recovery; it is a new
--           trusted rule and is deliberately NOT taken here.
--   other   unchanged `Nothing` (field-identity Phase 4 review F3).
--
-- The trailing `else Just false` is DEAD over the whole closed `tsKind` image
-- and is left as a receipt rather than fenced: `subsetWK` intercepts union /
-- intersect / complement on both sides, `subsetWKBase` intercepts refined,
-- `subsetWKLeaf` peels opaque, `ssSameKind` takes named / variant / mu / tagged
-- and `ssSameKindTail` takes unit / app, so only record / arrow / map / tuple /
-- other can reach here and all five are named above.  A fence there would be
-- theater; the invariant is the unreachability.
@label "subset: ssCompositeSound"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b / type-substrate P1(a.7) — the SOUND-mode composite arm. Record keeps the fully gated width+depth rule. Tuple is POSITIVE-ONLY: its arity and slot refutations carried a measured false definite (no have-nonemptiness gate, so a Void-factor tuple refuted while its denotation is empty at both the conceptual reading and the implemented decomposeMatchesTuple face) and its item axis bottoms out in accept-all/refuse-all degrades. Arrow and map ABSTAIN in both polarities: every arrow verdict is refuted at validation's non-circular paramCount axis and by the flatten/written-arity divergence, and ssMap's partial-dictionary key rule contradicts validationValidateMap's total-length finite arm. The unknown kind abstains; the trailing Just false is unreachable over the closed tsKind image and is kept as a receipt. Internal helper to ssComposite."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssCompositeSound : (picker: Boolean) -> (k: String) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssCompositeSound picker k have want =
  if eq k "record" then recordSubGated picker (tsRecordFields have) (tsRecordFields want)
  else if eq k "arrow" then Nothing
  else if eq k "tuple" then ttKeepTrue (tupleSub picker (tsTupleItems have) (tsTupleItems want))
  else if eq k "map" then Nothing
  -- field-identity Phase 4 (review F3) — the UNDECIDABLE kind abstains in the
  -- SOUND judgment: a same-kind TtUnknown pair (e.g. a `$refined` whose set the
  -- boundary does not recognize — deliberately unknown-NOT-invalid per the
  -- three-way posture) previously fell into the refuting tail, violating
  -- reflexivity (subset(X, X) = Just false for an unrecognized refinement).
  -- The PICKER tail keeps its frozen Just false — a presentation filter, not a
  -- judgment (ssCompositePicker's oracle-pinned coarsening).
  else if eq k "other" then Nothing
  else Just false

-- ⚠ RETIRED FROM SOUND MODE at type-substrate P1(a.7) — UNREACHED.
-- `ssCompositeSound`'s map arm now abstains, and the picker never enters this
-- function (`ssCompositePicker` answers at constructor level).  It stays
-- REGISTERED rather than deleted because removing a registered id mints a new
-- identity row and invalidates both compiled-artifact certificates; it is the
-- anchor for the future map-recovery slice (a key-EQUALITY-gated positive, the
-- `conformMap` rule, which is reading-invariant where this partial-dictionary
-- rule is not).  Do NOT re-point a sound caller at it without re-litigating the
-- entitlement.
@label "subset: ssMap"
@description "Phase 5 (S-mapkeys) / type-substrate P1(a.7) — the partial-dictionary map ⊆ rule: Map<K1,V1> ⊆ Map<K2,V2> iff K1 ⊆ K2 (decideSubset over the carried key SetExprs) AND V1 ⊆ V2 (covariant). UNREACHED from sound mode as of P1(a.7): its key rule contradicts validationValidateMap's total-length finite arm, which accepts a length-3 array only on the have side of Map[3,T] ⊆ Map[4,T], so the positive was face-false at an implemented arm. Retained registered as the anchor for the key-equality recovery slice. Internal helper, currently no caller."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
ssMap : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssMap picker have want =
  mAnd (decideSubset (tsMapKeys have) (tsMapKeys want)) (subsetW picker (tsMapValues have) (tsMapValues want))

@label "subset: ssMaybeCongruent"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — picker retains the inclusive legacy tsMaybeInner extraction and fall-through. Sound mode requires exact typeTraversalMaybeInner on both operands and retains only a recursive Just true; inner refutations/unknowns abstain because Maybe forwards non-tagged values."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssMaybeCongruent : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssMaybeCongruent picker have want =
  if picker then ssMaybeCongruentPicker picker have want else ssMaybeCongruentSound have want

@category "engine-internal"
ssMaybeCongruentPicker : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssMaybeCongruentPicker picker have want =
  case tsMaybeInner have of
    Nothing -> Just true
    Just hi ->
      case tsMaybeInner want of
        Nothing -> Just true
        Just wi -> subsetW picker hi wi

@category "engine-internal"
ssMaybeCongruentSound : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ssMaybeCongruentSound have want = case ttExactMaybeInner have of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just hi -> case ttExactMaybeInner want of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just wi -> ttKeepTrue (subsetW false hi wi)

-- ── Step 2b — the SOUND-mode component-wise machinery ───────────────────────
-- A Kleene `Tri` conjunction + head/tail list-walkers over the marshalled
-- field / case / item / param lists (the `head`/`tail` Maybe-native idiom — the
-- array-repr List does not pattern-match Nil/Cons). Reached ONLY in SOUND mode
-- (`picker = False`); the picker-mode arms never call them ⇒ the FunctionPicker
-- oracle is byte-green by construction.

-- mAnd — Kleene AND over Tri: a `Just false` dominates (false ∧ x = false), then
-- `Nothing` (undecided), then `Just true`. The composite folds combine per-element
-- verdicts through this.
@label "subset: mAnd"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — Kleene conjunction over Tri (Maybe Bool): Just false dominates (∧ false = false); Just true ⇒ the other; Nothing ⇒ Nothing unless the other is Just false. The component-wise folds' combiner. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
mAnd : (a: Maybe Boolean) -> (b: Maybe Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
mAnd a b = case a of
  Nothing -> mAndNothing b
  Just av -> if av then b else Just false

@label "subset: mAndNothing"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the Nothing-left case of mAnd: Nothing ∧ Just false = Just false (false dominates), else Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
mAndNothing : (b: Maybe Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
mAndNothing b = case b of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just bv -> if bv then Nothing else Just false

-- ssRest / emptyList — the shared list-walk primitives (over the array-repr List
-- via the `tail`/`head` Maybe natives). `ssRest` = the tail-or-`[]`; `emptyList`
-- = `Just true` iff the list is empty (the arity/exhaustion check).
@label "subset: ssRest"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the tail of a list, or [] when empty (tail Nothing → []). The recursion step for the component-wise walks. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
ssRest : (xs: List a) -> List a
ssRest xs = case tail xs of
  Nothing -> []
  Just r -> r

@label "subset: emptyList"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — Just true iff the list is empty, else Just false (the tuple/arrow arity-exhaustion check). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyList : (xs: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyList xs = case head xs of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just x -> Just false

-- ── marshalled-shape accessors (TtRecord / TtVariant / TtArrow / TtTuple / TtMap
-- + their TtField / TtVariantCase / TtArrowParam sub-records) ────────────────

@label "subset: tsRecordFields"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the field list of a TtRecord (else []). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsRecordFields : (t: a) -> List b
tsRecordFields t = case t of
  TtRecord { fields = fs } -> fs
  _ -> []

@label "subset: tsVariantCases"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the case list of a TtVariant (else []). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsVariantCases : (t: a) -> List b
tsVariantCases t = case t of
  TtVariant { cases = cs } -> cs
  _ -> []

@label "subset: tsTupleItems"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the item-type list of a TtTuple (else []). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsTupleItems : (t: a) -> List b
tsTupleItems t = case t of
  TtTuple { items = is } -> is
  _ -> []

@label "subset: tsMapValues"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the value type of a TtMap (else passthrough). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsMapValues : (t: a) -> b
tsMapValues t = case t of
  TtMap { values = v } -> v
  _ -> t

@label "subset: tsMapKeys"
@description "Phase 5 (S-mapkeys) — the allowed-key SetExpr carried on a TtMap (the marshaller defaults an unconstrained map to the universe {$all}); passed opaquely to set:decideSubset for the map-key-domain ⊆ check. Else passthrough. Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
tsMapKeys : (t: a) -> b
tsMapKeys t = case t of
  TtMap { keys = k } -> k
  _ -> t

@label "subset: tsArrowParams"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the param list (TtArrowParam) of a TtArrow (else []). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsArrowParams : (t: a) -> List b
tsArrowParams t = case t of
  TtArrow { params = ps } -> ps
  _ -> []

@label "subset: tsArrowReturns"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the return type of a TtArrow (else passthrough). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsArrowReturns : (t: a) -> b
tsArrowReturns t = case t of
  TtArrow { returns = r } -> r
  _ -> t

@label "subset: tsFieldKey"
@description "Field-identity Phase 3 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — the validated semantic FieldKey of a TtField. Named keys carry UUID-backed FieldRefs and positional keys carry ordinals; embedded and scoped-effective wires are separate face coordinates, never identity."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "field-identity" "phase-3"
@category "engine-internal"
tsFieldKey : (f: a) -> b
tsFieldKey f = case f of
  TtField { semanticKey = k } -> k
  _ -> f

@label "subset: tsFieldType"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the type of a TtField (else passthrough). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsFieldType : (f: a) -> b
tsFieldType f = case f of
  TtField { type = t } -> t
  _ -> f

@label "subset: tsFieldRaw"
@description "Phase 5 (E-erasable) — the RAW (un-marshalled) FenelType of a TtField (else passthrough); passed to the isErasableType ctx-native (the Undefinable dispatch needs the raw `$`-keyed type, not the marshalled view). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
tsFieldRaw : (f: a) -> b
tsFieldRaw f = case f of
  TtField { raw = r } -> r
  _ -> f

@label "subset: tsCaseName"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the name of a TtVariantCase (else \"\"). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsCaseName : (c: a) -> String
tsCaseName c = case c of
  TtVariantCase { name = n } -> n
  _ -> ""

@label "subset: tsCaseFields"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the field list of a TtVariantCase payload (else []). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsCaseFields : (c: a) -> List b
tsCaseFields c = case c of
  TtVariantCase { fields = fs } -> fs
  _ -> []

@label "subset: tsParamType"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the type of a TtArrowParam (else passthrough). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsParamType : (p: a) -> b
tsParamType p = case p of
  TtArrowParam { type = t } -> t
  _ -> p

-- ── record (width + depth) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- have <: want iff EVERY want-field is present in have with subset (covariant,
-- depth); extra have-fields are fine (width). Iterate want-fields.

@label "subset: recordSub"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b / type-substrate P1(a.6) — record width/depth fold entered only through recordSubGated's complete keyed-product face fence. Matching uses semantic FieldKey and covariant occurrence type; extra have axes remain open-record axes."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
recordSub : (picker: Boolean) -> (hfs: List a) -> (wfs: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
recordSub picker hfs wfs = case head wfs of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just wf -> mAnd (recordFieldSub picker hfs wf) (recordSub picker hfs (ssRest wfs))

@label "subset: recordSubGated"
@description "field-identity Phase 4 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — shared record/variant-payload wrapper. Before any width, depth, optionality, or inhabitance verdict, both complete products must pass scoped-effective and embedded coordinate injectivity/alignment, reserved-wire, eager child-plan, and enforcing-widget occurrence checks. A surviving Just false still consults product emptiness so an empty have is vacuously contained."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "field-identity" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
recordSubGated : (picker: Boolean) -> (hfs: List a) -> (wfs: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
recordSubGated picker hfs wfs =
  if not (ttProductPairReady hfs wfs "" "")
  then Nothing
  else case recordSub picker hfs wfs of
    Just false ->
      case anyEmpty false hfs of
        Just true -> Just true
        Just false -> Just false
        Nothing -> Nothing
    v -> v

@label "subset: recordFieldSub"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b / type-substrate P1(a.6) — one already-gated want axis. A present semantic FieldKey checks optionality and covariant depth. An absent erasable want key now abstains: omission permission does not constrain an extra property admitted by the open have record. An absent required key retains the witness-graded refutation, with embedded-wire ambiguity conservative and have-inhabitance handled by recordSubGated."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
recordFieldSub : (picker: Boolean) -> (hfs: List a) -> (wf: b) -> Maybe Boolean
recordFieldSub picker hfs wf = case findFieldByKey hfs (tsFieldKey wf) of
  Nothing ->
    if fieldsShareWireName hfs (tsFieldWireName wf)
    then Nothing
    else if isErasableType (tsFieldRaw wf)
      then Nothing
      else Just false
  Just hf -> recordFieldDepth picker hf wf

@label "subset: recordFieldDepth"
@description "Phase 5 (E-erasable) — the present-field verdict of recordFieldSub (have HAS the want-field): if the want-field is REQUIRED (not Undefinable) but the have-field is Undefinable (erasable) ⇒ Just false (have may lack the value); else covariant subset on the field types. Reproduces isSubtype's `!bErasable && aErasable ⇒ false` record-depth gate (the Undefinable dispatch via isErasableType over the raw field types). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
recordFieldDepth : (picker: Boolean) -> (hf: a) -> (wf: b) -> Maybe Boolean
recordFieldDepth picker hf wf =
  if eraseMismatch (isErasableType (tsFieldRaw wf)) (isErasableType (tsFieldRaw hf))
    then Just false
    else subsetW picker (tsFieldType hf) (tsFieldType wf)

@label "subset: eraseMismatch"
@description "Phase 5 (E-erasable) — the record-depth optionality refutation: true iff the want-field is REQUIRED (wantErasable false) AND the have-field is erasable (haveErasable true) — a slot the supertype demands but the subtype may omit. Mirrors isSubtype's `!bErasable && aErasable`. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
eraseMismatch : (wantErasable: Boolean) -> (haveErasable: Boolean) -> Boolean
eraseMismatch wantErasable haveErasable = if wantErasable then false else haveErasable

@label "subset: findFieldByKey"
@description "Field-identity Phase 3 — find a validated TtField by semantic FieldKey. fieldKeyEq compares named UUIDs or positional ordinals; wire names never participate. Internal helper shared by record and named/positional variant payload reasoning."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "field-identity" "phase-3"
@category "engine-internal"
findFieldByKey : (fs: List a) -> (key: b) -> Maybe a
findFieldByKey fs key = case head fs of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just f -> if fieldKeyEq (tsFieldKey f) key then Just f else findFieldByKey (ssRest fs) key

@label "subset: tsFieldWireName"
@description "Field-identity Phase 3 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — the embedded wire snapshot of a TtField, never the scoped current projection and never identity. The complete face fence compares embedded and effective coordinates separately before this residual missing-key ambiguity check."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "field-identity" "phase-3"
@category "engine-internal"
tsFieldWireName : (f: a) -> String
tsFieldWireName f = case f of
  TtField { wireName = w } -> w
  _ -> ""

@label "subset: fieldsShareWireName"
@description "Field-identity Phase 3 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — whether any field carries this embedded wire snapshot. Empty never matches. This is only the residual missing-key ambiguity check after the complete dual-coordinate product fence."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "field-identity" "phase-3"
@category "engine-internal"
fieldsShareWireName : (fs: List a) -> (wireName: String) -> Boolean
fieldsShareWireName fs wireName =
  if eq wireName ""
  then false
  else case head fs of
    Nothing -> false
    Just f -> if eq (tsFieldWireName f) wireName then true else fieldsShareWireName (ssRest fs) wireName

-- ── variant (case-wise) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- have <: want iff EVERY have-case is present in want (by tag) with the case
-- payload ⊆ (have may have FEWER cases). Iterate have-cases; reuse recordSub for
-- each matched case's payload (a product).

@label "subset: variantSub"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — variant case-wise ⊆: every have-case present in want-cases (by tag) with its payload subset; have may have fewer cases. Folds mAnd over the have-cases. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
variantSub : (picker: Boolean) -> (hcs: List a) -> (wcs: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
variantSub picker hcs wcs = case head hcs of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just hc -> mAnd (variantCaseSub picker hc wcs) (variantSub picker (ssRest hcs) wcs)

@label "subset: variantCaseSub"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b / field-identity Phase 3+4 — one have-case's verdict: find a want-case of the same tag; present ⇒ variantPayloadSub with named UUID and positional-ordinal alignment. An ABSENT tag refutes only when the have-case is INHABITED (review F2: a case whose payload product is empty contributes ∅ to the have sum — its absence from want cannot witness non-containment); provably-empty ⇒ Just true for this case, undecided ⇒ Nothing. Case tags remain names. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
variantCaseSub : (picker: Boolean) -> (hc: a) -> (wcs: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
variantCaseSub picker hc wcs = case findCaseByName wcs (tsCaseName hc) of
  Nothing ->
    case anyEmpty false (tsCaseFields hc) of
      Just true -> Just true
      Just false -> Just false
      Nothing -> Nothing
  Just wc -> variantPayloadSub picker (tsCaseFields hc) (tsCaseFields wc)

@label "subset: variantPayloadSub"
@description "Phase 5 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — matched variant payloads reuse recordSubGated, including the full dual-coordinate plan/occurrence fence, semantic-FieldKey depth alignment, open-product absent-erasable abstention, and empty-have vacuity gate."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-5"
@category "engine-internal"
variantPayloadSub : (picker: Boolean) -> (hfs: List a) -> (wfs: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
variantPayloadSub picker hfs wfs = recordSubGated picker hfs wfs

@label "subset: findCaseByName"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b — the first case in a list whose name (tag) equals the given name (Maybe case). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
findCaseByName : (cs: List a) -> (name: String) -> Maybe a
findCaseByName cs name = case head cs of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just c -> if eq (tsCaseName c) name then Just c else findCaseByName (ssRest cs) name

-- ── tuple (pairwise) + arrow (variance) ─────────────────────────────────────

@label "subset: tupleSub"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b / type-substrate P1(a.7) — tuple pairwise ⊆: zip items, subset each positionally (covariant); length mismatch ⇒ Just false. TEXTUALLY UNCHANGED at P1(a.7) BY DESIGN: picker-mode ssApp folds its type-application args through this same function, so a fence written here would move picker decisions. The SOUND caller (ssCompositeSound) wraps it in ttKeepTrue instead, which retires both the arity and the slot refutation — they carry no have-nonemptiness gate, so a Void-factor tuple refuted while its denotation is empty. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tupleSub : (picker: Boolean) -> (his: List a) -> (wis: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
tupleSub picker his wis = case head his of
  Nothing -> emptyList wis
  Just hi ->
    case head wis of
      Nothing -> Just false
      Just wi -> mAnd (subsetW picker hi wi) (tupleSub picker (ssRest his) (ssRest wis))

-- ⚠ RETIRED FROM SOUND MODE at type-substrate P1(a.7) — UNREACHED, together
-- with its whole helper family (ttArrowFlatten, ttArrowAligned,
-- ttArrowArityTail, ttArrowCallableRefute, ttRefuteIfNonempty, ttCallableFree,
-- ttAtomName, ttAtomNameKnown, someParamEmptyW, arrowSubVariance, paramsSub).
-- `ssCompositeSound`'s arrow arm now abstains and the picker answers at
-- constructor level, so nothing calls this.  It stays REGISTERED rather than
-- deleted because removing a registered id mints an identity row and
-- invalidates both compiled-artifact certificates; it is the anchor for the
-- future arrow-recovery slice.  It has THREE `Just true` emitters, not two —
-- the `someParamEmptyW` vacuity short-circuit, the `∅ ⊆ want` short-circuit off
-- `emptyArrow`, and `arrowSubVariance` — and the first is refuted by
-- validation's `paramCount` axis (witness `"std:negate"` against a 2-param
-- want), so any future `ttKeepTrue` of this arm must enumerate all three and
-- entitle each independently.
@label "subset: arrowSub"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b / decide-substrate 8λ.1-r / 8λ.2-r / floor-kernel Phase 2 / type-substrate P1(a.7) — arrow variance (north-star §6), CURRY-NORMALIZED + EMPTINESS-GATED on BOTH SIDES. UNREACHED from sound mode as of P1(a.7) (two implemented refuters survive every verdict: validation's registered-name paramCount, and the flatten-vs-written-arity divergence); retained registered as the arrow-recovery anchor. Phase-2 STOP-clause soundness fix (the F-differential reconciliation): both sides FLATTEN first (ttArrowFlatten — the 8λ.2-r Se* arrowFlatten mirrored onto the Tt* face; ⟦(A,B)→C⟧ = ⟦(A)→((B)→C)⟧ under the currying calling convention, so the old written-arity refutation of a flat-vs-curried pair was a false Just false where setAlgebraSubsetArrowArm proves Just true). Then: (1) a WANT-arrow with SOME param type decidably EMPTY (someParamEmptyW — e.g. `(Void)→X`) ⇒ Just true UNCONDITIONALLY (`∀x∈∅` holds vacuously for every callable); (2) a decidably-EMPTY have-arrow (emptyArrow) ⇒ Just true (∅ ⊆ want — the 8λ.1-r find); else EQUAL flattened arities take the variance verdict (arrowSubVariance, its Just-false gated on the have-arrow being decidably NONEMPTY) and RESIDUAL arity mismatches take the gated callable-tail refutation (ttArrowArityTail — all want-params provably inhabited ∧ the shorter side's codomain provably callable-free, the setAlgebraArrowSubAligned mirror; else Nothing). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6" "floor-kernel" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
arrowSub : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
arrowSub picker have want =
  let haveF = ttArrowFlatten have
  let wantF = ttArrowFlatten want
  if someParamEmptyW (tsArrowParams wantF) then Just true
  else
    case emptyArrow false haveF of
      Just true -> Just true
      Just false -> ttArrowAligned picker haveF wantF true
      Nothing -> ttArrowAligned picker haveF wantF false

@label "subset: ttArrowFlatten"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 2 (STOP-clause soundness fix) — CURRY-NORMALIZE a TtArrow: while the return type is itself a TtArrow, pull its params up (`TtArrow ps (TtArrow qs r)` ⇒ `TtArrow (ps++qs) r`). The Tt* twin of the Se* arrowFlatten (decide-substrate 8λ.2-r): sound at the value-set level because Fenel's calling convention curries both ways, so the flat and curried spellings denote the SAME set of function values. Non-TtArrow ⇒ unchanged. Internal helper to arrowSub."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "arrow" "floor-kernel" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
ttArrowFlatten : (t: a) -> a
ttArrowFlatten t = case t of
  TtArrow { params = ps, returns = r, raw = rw } ->
    case r of
      TtArrow { params = qs } ->
        ttArrowFlatten (TtArrow { params = concat ps qs, returns = tsArrowReturns r, raw = rw })
      _ -> t
  _ -> t

@label "subset: ttArrowAligned"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 2 (STOP-clause soundness fix) — the post-flatten arity dispatch of arrowSub (the setAlgebraArrowSubAligned Tt* mirror): EQUAL flattened arities ⇒ the variance core (arrowSubVariance, nonemptyKnown-gated); arities STILL mismatched after flattening ⇒ the gated callable-tail refutation (ttArrowArityTail). Internal helper to arrowSub."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "arrow" "floor-kernel" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
ttArrowAligned : (picker: Boolean) -> (haveF: a) -> (wantF: a) -> (nonemptyKnown: Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
ttArrowAligned picker haveF wantF nonemptyKnown =
  if eq (length (tsArrowParams haveF)) (length (tsArrowParams wantF))
  then arrowSubVariance picker haveF wantF nonemptyKnown
  else ttArrowArityTail haveF wantF nonemptyKnown

@label "subset: ttArrowArityTail"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 2 (STOP-clause soundness fix) — the residual-arity-mismatch refutation, FULLY GATED (the setAlgebraArrowSubAligned mirror): every want-param must be PROVABLY inhabited (paramsInhab Just true — else the ∀ may be vacuous ⇒ Nothing, the gate the want-vacuous Just-true above makes near-complete), then a longer-have member applied to fewer args is a PARTIAL (a callable) ⇒ a provably CALLABLE-FREE want-codomain refutes, and a shorter-have member's value after its params lies in the have-codomain ⇒ provably CALLABLE-FREE ⇒ it cannot absorb the remaining want-args ⇒ refutes; both refutations still ride the caller's have-NONEMPTY gate (ttRefuteIfNonempty). A codomain not provably callable-free ⇒ Nothing (the refutation softens — e.g. a named alias that could denote an arrow type). Internal helper to ttArrowAligned."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "arrow" "floor-kernel" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
ttArrowArityTail : (haveF: a) -> (wantF: a) -> (nonemptyKnown: Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
ttArrowArityTail haveF wantF nonemptyKnown =
  if not (containmentProven (paramsInhab false (tsArrowParams wantF)))
  then Nothing
  else if gt (length (tsArrowParams haveF)) (length (tsArrowParams wantF))
  then ttArrowCallableRefute (tsArrowReturns wantF) nonemptyKnown
  else ttArrowCallableRefute (tsArrowReturns haveF) nonemptyKnown

@label "subset: ttArrowCallableRefute"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 2 (STOP-clause soundness fix) — the callable-free-codomain leg of the arity refutation: the given codomain provably callable-free (ttCallableFree) ⇒ refute gated on the have-arrow's known nonemptiness; else Nothing. Internal helper to ttArrowArityTail."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "arrow" "floor-kernel" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
ttArrowCallableRefute : (codomain: a) -> (nonemptyKnown: Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
ttArrowCallableRefute codomain nonemptyKnown =
  if ttCallableFree codomain
  then ttRefuteIfNonempty nonemptyKnown
  else Nothing

@label "subset: ttRefuteIfNonempty"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 2 — Just false only when the have-arrow is decidably NONEMPTY (a maybe-empty have is still ⊆ — honest Nothing); the arrowSubVariance nonemptyKnown gate shared by the arity tail. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "arrow" "floor-kernel" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
ttRefuteIfNonempty : (nonemptyKnown: Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
ttRefuteIfNonempty nonemptyKnown =
  if nonemptyKnown then Just false else Nothing

@label "subset: ttCallableFree"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 2 (STOP-clause soundness fix) — is a marshalled TYPE provably free of callable values (the check.fenel checkCallableFree posture, Tt*-side): $void ⇒ true (empty); a KNOWN atom-tower nominal name (TtNamed / TtOpaque via nominalNameOf + emptyNamed — numbers/strings/chars/bools are never callable) ⇒ true; refined ⇒ its base (refined ⊆ base); opaque ⇒ its pure view; everything else (arrow / var / unknown alias / record — a closure object could inhabit an open record) ⇒ false (the refutation softens). Internal helper to ttArrowCallableRefute."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "arrow" "floor-kernel" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
ttCallableFree : (t: a) -> Boolean
ttCallableFree t =
  if tsIsVoid t then true
  else if ttAtomName (nominalNameOf t) then true
  else if eq (tsKind t) "refined" then ttCallableFree (tsBase t)
  else if eq (tsKind t) "opaque" then ttCallableFree (tsPure t)
  else false

@label "subset: ttAtomName"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 2 — does a Maybe nominal-name resolve to a KNOWN inhabited atom-tower name (emptyNamed = Just false)? The Tt* twin of checkCallableFree's SeRef arm. Internal helper to ttCallableFree."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "arrow" "floor-kernel" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
ttAtomName : (mn: a) -> Boolean
ttAtomName mn = case mn of
  Nothing -> false
  Just n -> ttAtomNameKnown (emptyNamed n)

@label "subset: ttAtomNameKnown"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 2 — the emptyNamed verdict → callable-free gate: Just false (a known-inhabited atom) ⇒ true; Just true / Nothing ⇒ false. Internal helper to ttAtomName."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "arrow" "floor-kernel" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
ttAtomNameKnown : (m: a) -> Boolean
ttAtomNameKnown m = case m of
  Just b -> not b
  Nothing -> false

@label "subset: someParamEmptyW"
@description "decide-substrate 8λ.2-r — does SOME arrow param have a decidably-EMPTY type (emptyW = Just true)? The want-side vacuous gate for arrowSub: a want-arrow with an uninhabitable param domain is never invocable, so EVERY function value is vacuously a member (∀x∈∅) — the Tt* twin of the judgment's arrowSomeParamEmpty. ⚠ NOT INFORMATION-MONOTONE, and a successor must know this before re-reaching `arrowSub` (type-substrate P1(a.8), found by post-commit adversarial review). This returns a BOOLEAN, so it reads `Nothing` as \"keep going\" rather than as \"stop, unknown\": when a leaf loses a definite the short-circuit stops firing and a DIFFERENT rule decides, which can FLIP the polarity rather than soften it. Derived at P1(a.8) entry vs measured after: `arrowSub(TRUE, (Number)→Number, (tagged{value=void})→String)` was `Just true` via this gate and is `Just false` via variance — PICKER mode specifically; `arrowSub(false, …)` returns `Nothing` post-repair, so the flip is not a sound-mode one, because the tagged emptiness peel was retired. Nothing ships from that — `arrowSub` has been UNREACHED from sound dispatch since P1(a.7) and the P1(a.8) differential measures ZERO non-monotone movements across 8757 public columns — but the arrow-recovery slice may NOT simply re-point `ssCompositeSound` here: this gate must first propagate `Nothing` as `Nothing`. Ledger `t.emp.arrow`. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "decide-substrate" "phase-8lambda"
@category "engine-internal"
someParamEmptyW : (ps: List a) -> Boolean
someParamEmptyW ps = case head ps of
  Nothing -> false
  Just p ->
    case emptyW false (tsParamType p) of
      Just b -> if b then true else someParamEmptyW (ssRest ps)
      Nothing -> someParamEmptyW (ssRest ps)

@label "subset: arrowSubVariance"
@description "decide-substrate 8λ.1-r — arrowSub's variance core: (p1->r1) ⊆ (p2->r2) iff params CONTRAVARIANT (want-params ⊆ have-params, pairwise) AND result COVARIANT (have-return ⊆ want-return). `nonemptyKnown` (the caller's emptyArrow verdict) gates a Just-false: only a decidably-NONEMPTY have-arrow certifies the refutation witness (a maybe-empty have ⇒ honest Nothing). Internal helper to arrowSub."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "structural-dispatch" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
arrowSubVariance : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (want: a) -> (nonemptyKnown: Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
arrowSubVariance picker have want nonemptyKnown =
  let paramsOk = paramsSub picker (tsArrowParams want) (tsArrowParams have)
  let returnsOk = subsetW picker (tsArrowReturns have) (tsArrowReturns want)
  case mAnd paramsOk returnsOk of
    Just true -> Just true
    Just false -> if nonemptyKnown then Just false else Nothing
    Nothing -> Nothing

@label "subset: paramsSub"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2b / field-identity Phase 3 — the contravariant pairwise param fold for arrowSub: zip the two param lists strictly by list position and subset their types (callers pass want first). Param FieldKeys survive as metadata but never reorder variance; flattened curried arrows may therefore contain repeated local positional ordinals. Arity mismatch ⇒ Just false. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
paramsSub : (picker: Boolean) -> (wps: List a) -> (hps: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
paramsSub picker wps hps = case head wps of
  Nothing -> emptyList hps
  Just wp ->
    case head hps of
      Nothing -> Just false
      Just hp -> mAnd (subsetW picker (tsParamType wp) (tsParamType hp)) (paramsSub picker (ssRest wps) (ssRest hps))

-- ── Step 1b — the tier-2 former subset arms ($union / $intersect / $complement)
-- All reuse the SAME deciders the leaf arms call (mAnd / mOr / emTrueOnly +
-- subsetW recursion + ttDisjoint → decideDisjoint). NO containment-private
-- theory list — the structural arms surface the existing deciders (design-lock
-- §4). SOUND throughout: a positive ⊆ proof is only emitted when genuinely
-- provable; otherwise Nothing (never a fabricated Just false).

@label "subset: subsetUnionHave"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — LHS union ⊆: (A ∪ B) ⊆ want iff EVERY branch ⊆ want (mAnd-fold of subsetW over the union branches). Sound AND complete. An empty branch list ⇒ Just true (∪∅ = ∅ ⊆ anything). Internal helper to subsetWK."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetUnionHave : (picker: Boolean) -> (branches: List a) -> (want: b) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetUnionHave picker branches want = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just b -> mAnd (subsetW picker b want) (subsetUnionHave picker (ssRest branches) want)

@label "subset: subsetUnionWant"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — RHS union ⊆: have ⊆ (A ∪ B) when have ⊆ SOME branch (∃). Just true if any branch positively proves, else Nothing (a non-match does NOT refute — have may split across branches). emTrueOnly drops each branch's Just false; mOr-fold keeps the positive. Internal helper to subsetWK."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetUnionWant : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (branches: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetUnionWant picker have branches = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b -> mOr (emTrueOnly (subsetW picker have b)) (subsetUnionWant picker have (ssRest branches))

@label "subset: subsetIntersectHave"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — LHS intersect ⊆: (A ∩ B) ⊆ want when SOME branch ⊆ want (∃; A∩B ⊆ A, so a branch ⊆ want proves the whole). Just true if any branch proves, else Nothing. Internal helper to subsetWK."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetIntersectHave : (picker: Boolean) -> (branches: List a) -> (want: b) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetIntersectHave picker branches want = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b -> mOr (emTrueOnly (subsetW picker b want)) (subsetIntersectHave picker (ssRest branches) want)

@label "subset: subsetIntersectWant"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — RHS intersect ⊆: have ⊆ (A ∩ B) iff have ⊆ EVERY branch (∀; mAnd-fold of subsetW). Sound AND complete. An empty branch list ⇒ Just true (∩∅ = ⊤). Internal helper to subsetWK."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
subsetIntersectWant : (picker: Boolean) -> (have: a) -> (branches: List b) -> Maybe Boolean
subsetIntersectWant picker have branches = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just b -> mAnd (subsetW picker have b) (subsetIntersectWant picker have (ssRest branches))

-- ── floor-kernel Phase 3c — Tt Boolean normalization + top-equivalence ──────
-- The Tt* mirror of setAlgebraNnf/setAlgebraTopCover. It deliberately shares
-- subsetW/emptyW/disjoint rather than duplicating predicate theory. NNF leaves
-- complements immediately above non-Boolean leaves. A top-cover pairing then
-- removes one complement branch and asks subsetW on its complement-free inner,
-- so the top-cover↔subset composition terminates on the number of remaining
-- complement literals plus structural size.

@label "containment: ttNnf"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — convert TraversalType union/intersection/complement formers to negation normal form with a parity bit; complements remain only above non-Boolean leaves. Synthetic nodes retain an opaque raw seed that no containment rule inspects. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "normalize" "nnf" "complement" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttNnf : (t: a) -> a
ttNnf t = ttNnfPolarity t false

@label "containment: ttNnfPolarity"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — parity-threaded Tt NNF worker. Union/intersection swap under odd parity; complement flips parity; a negated leaf becomes TtComplement. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "normalize" "nnf" "complement" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttNnfPolarity : (t: a) -> (negated: Boolean) -> a
ttNnfPolarity t negated = case t of
  TtUnion { branches = bs, raw = rw } ->
    let ns = ttNnfList bs negated
    if negated then TtIntersect { branches = ns, raw = rw } else TtUnion { branches = ns, raw = rw }
  TtIntersect { branches = bs, raw = rw } ->
    let ns = ttNnfList bs negated
    if negated then TtUnion { branches = ns, raw = rw } else TtIntersect { branches = ns, raw = rw }
  TtComplement { inner = i } -> ttNnfPolarity i (not negated)
  _ -> if negated then TtComplement { inner = t, raw = t } else t

@label "containment: ttNnfList"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — map ttNnfPolarity over a TraversalType branch list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "normalize" "nnf" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttNnfList : (branches: List a) -> (negated: Boolean) -> List a
ttNnfList branches negated = case head branches of
  Nothing -> []
  Just b -> concat [ttNnfPolarity b negated] (ttNnfList (ssRest branches) negated)

@label "containment: ttTopCover"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c / type-substrate P1(a.5) — exact Tt top-equivalence slice: complement leaf via inner emptiness; intersection by Kleene every; union by an already-top branch or P∪¬N=top iff N⊆P; void/known named/rigid structural leaves are provably proper EXCEPT `$map` and `$variant`, whose kinds cannot prove properness — an enum-keyed `$map`'s validation arm accepts ANY value identically, and canonical `Maybe` is a bare `$variant` that FORWARDS an untagged value to its inner type, so `Maybe (Map<enum,_>)` accepts everything measured; refined delegates to its base and, only when the base is top, to decideSubset top set. **type-substrate P1(a.8): the `$tagged` peel is RETIRED — this face now abstains for `$tagged` in every polarity (ledger `t.top.tagged`), because validation reads a `$tagged` by UUID syntax only while `matchesShape` recurses into the value slot, so top-cover reasoning about that slot reasons about a population no single face implements.** Anything else is Nothing. ⚠ RESIDUAL, RESTATED AND NOW MEASURED — the previous wording (\"no such type exists in the corpus and none is a measured defect\") is RETRACTED as inaccurate: this face still peels `$opaque` without tracking it (the `rp` flag exists only on `disjointW`), and an `$opaque` whose pure view is `¬$void` EXECUTES through the marshal boundary and was READ as defeating both polarities (rounds 9-10 showed it defeats neither — see below). MEASURED at P1(a.8) entry with `O = $opaque{name, pure = ¬$void}`: `empty(O)` = `Just false`, `empty(¬O)` = `Just true`, `sub(¬O, $void)` = `Just true`, while `matchesShape(0, ¬O)` = `true` and `validate(O, 0)` is INVALID — ⚠ but rounds 9 and 10 narrowed this to almost nothing, and the honest reading is now: that `true` comes from decompose's complement WILDCARD (context, not evidence); `validate` refuses every value of every complement except the exact universal `¬$void` (`Anything`, which it accepts), so it says nothing here either; and under the `pure` reading `empty(¬O) = Just true` is CORRECT. `t.top.opaque` is SIDE-CONDITIONED, not an executed false definite: the OPEN question is TOPNESS DISAGREEMENT — an opaque whose `pure` view and whose live carrier disagree on whether they COVER ⊤ — and no such witness exists yet. ⚠ NOT merely a carrier split: `Int` is one (`pure` a `$record`, inhabitants host NUMBERS) and `empty(¬Int) = Just false` is SOUND, because both sides are proper subsets of ⊤. This arm only ever emits \"is ⊤\" / \"is not ⊤\", so a split on the same side of ⊤ is invisible to it. It is a DIFFERENT shape from this phase's wrapper family (the `$opaque` carrier, not the `$tagged` denotation split), so under that phase's stop rule 2 it is FILED (ledger `t.top.opaque`) rather than repaired here. Internal helper shared by complement subset and emptiness."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "empty" "top-cover" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttTopCover : (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ttTopCover t =
  if tsIsVoid t then Just false
  else if eq (tsKind t) "opaque" then ttTopCover (tsPure t)
  else if eq (tsKind t) "tagged" then Nothing
  else if eq (tsKind t) "complement" then emptyW false (tsComplementInner t)
  else if eq (tsKind t) "intersect" then ttTopCoverEvery (tsIntersectBranches t)
  else if eq (tsKind t) "union" then ttTopCoverUnion (tsUnionBranches t)
  else if eq (tsKind t) "refined" then ttTopCoverRefined t
  else if eq (tsKind t) "named" then ttTopCoverNamed (tsName t)
  else if eq (tsKind t) "map" then Nothing
  else if eq (tsKind t) "variant" then Nothing
  else if ttRigidKind (tsKind t) then Just false
  else Nothing

@label "containment: ttTopCoverRefined"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — refined(base,set) top-cover: a proper base makes the refinement proper; a base already proven top delegates top⊆set to the shared SetExpr decider; an unknown base remains unknown. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "top-cover" "refined" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttTopCoverRefined : (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ttTopCoverRefined t = case ttTopCover (tsBase t) of
  Just false -> Just false
  Just true -> decideSubset SeAll (tsRefinedSet t)
  Nothing -> Nothing

@label "containment: ttTopCoverNamed"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — a name with a known value-domain category is a proper subset of the all-values universe; unknown aliases abstain. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "top-cover" "named" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttTopCoverNamed : (name: String) -> Maybe Boolean
ttTopCoverNamed name = case containmentNamedDomain name of
  Just d -> Just false
  Nothing -> Nothing

@label "containment: ttTopCoverEvery"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — top covers an intersection iff it covers every branch; empty intersection is top. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "top-cover" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttTopCoverEvery : (branches: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
ttTopCoverEvery branches = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just b -> mAnd (ttTopCover b) (ttTopCoverEvery (ssRest branches))

@label "containment: ttTopCoverUnion"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — top-cover a TtUnion: a top branch wins; otherwise scan complement pairings. Empty union is bottom and therefore proper; a nonempty union without a decided pairing remains Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "top-cover" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttTopCoverUnion : (branches: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
ttTopCoverUnion branches =
  if ttTopCoverAnyBranch branches then Just true
  else case ttTopCoverUnionPairs branches [] of
    Just b -> Just b
    Nothing -> if eq (length branches) 0 then Just false else Nothing

@label "containment: ttTopCoverAnyBranch"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — true iff some union branch independently has a Just-true top-cover proof. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "top-cover" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttTopCoverAnyBranch : (branches: List a) -> Boolean
ttTopCoverAnyBranch branches = case head branches of
  Nothing -> false
  Just b -> case ttTopCover b of
    Just true -> true
    _ -> ttTopCoverAnyBranch (ssRest branches)

@label "containment: ttTopCoverUnionPairs"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — scan an NNF TtUnion for ¬N and decide N⊆P where P is every other branch; a decided polarity is exact, while Nothing tries the next complement literal. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "top-cover" "subset" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttTopCoverUnionPairs : (remaining: List a) -> (prefix: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
ttTopCoverUnionPairs remaining prefix = case head remaining of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b ->
    let rest = ssRest remaining
    case b of
      TtComplement { inner = i } ->
        let others = concat prefix rest
        case ttTopCoverPair i others b of
          Just r -> Just r
          Nothing -> ttTopCoverUnionPairs rest (appendItem b prefix)
      _ -> ttTopCoverUnionPairs rest (appendItem b prefix)

@label "containment: ttTopCoverPair"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — one P∪¬N pairing: empty P asks emptyW N; otherwise ask subsetW N P, constructing only a synthetic TtUnion view when P has multiple branches. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "top-cover" "subset" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttTopCoverPair : (inner: a) -> (positive: List a) -> (rawSeed: a) -> Maybe Boolean
ttTopCoverPair inner positive rawSeed =
  if eq (length positive) 0
  then emptyW false inner
  else subsetW false inner (ttTopCoverUnionOf positive rawSeed)

@label "containment: ttTopCoverUnionOf"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — collapse a nonempty branch list to its singleton or a synthetic TtUnion for the pairing subset query. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "top-cover" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttTopCoverUnionOf : (branches: List a) -> (rawSeed: a) -> a
ttTopCoverUnionOf branches rawSeed =
  if eq (length branches) 1
  then fromMaybe rawSeed (head branches)
  else TtUnion { branches = branches, raw = rawSeed }

@label "subset: ttDisjoint"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 3c — the former separate refined-only Tt disjoint coarsening now delegates to the unified TraversalType disjoint member. Used by RHS complement subset and intersection emptiness; no second representation or predicate theory table remains. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "disjoint" "floor-kernel" "phase-3c"
@category "engine-internal"
ttDisjoint : (a: r) -> (b: s) -> Maybe Boolean
ttDisjoint a b = disjoint a b

@label "subset: tsUnionBranches"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — the branch list of a TtUnion (else []). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
tsUnionBranches : (t: a) -> List b
tsUnionBranches t = case t of
  TtUnion { branches = bs } -> bs
  _ -> []

@label "subset: tsIntersectBranches"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — the branch list of a TtIntersect (else []). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
tsIntersectBranches : (t: a) -> List b
tsIntersectBranches t = case t of
  TtIntersect { branches = bs } -> bs
  _ -> []

@label "subset: tsComplementInner"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — the inner type of a TtComplement (else passthrough). Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "subset" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
tsComplementInner : (t: a) -> a
tsComplementInner t = case t of
  TtComplement { inner = i } -> i
  _ -> t

-- subset — the SOUND containment member: ⟦have⟧ ⊆ ⟦want⟧ as a Tri, sound MODULO
-- the TCB ledger's open rows (`design/tcb-ledger.md`): `t.top.opaque` is a live
-- SIDE-CONDITIONED entry reachable from here (round 10 reclassified it — no
-- executed refutation exists), and `t.sub.resolve` is MISSING — its
-- co-induction condition is UNREACHABLE, so the arm emits nothing rather than
-- something wrong. (Round 9 corrected the class; `t.sub.resolve` was called
-- UNSOUND-KNOWN here, which it has not been since this phase repaired it.)
-- Available to
-- the prover, Phase 7, and the "subtype = subset" thesis (the precise sibling of
-- the picker-view typeSubsumes).
@label "Subset of types"
@description "set-algebra-to-fenel Phase 6 (containment capstone) Step 2 — `subset have want` decides whether ⟦have⟧ ⊆ ⟦want⟧ (every inhabitant of `have` is an inhabitant of `want`), returning Tri (Maybe Bool). The SOUND member of the containment relation — sound MODULO the TCB ledger's open rows (`t.top.opaque` is reachable from here) — = subsetW False: a type-variable expected slot ⇒ Nothing (undecidable); refined leaves surface set:decideSubset's Tri directly; refined/opaque layers transparent; named ⇒ nominal eq; Maybe ⇒ inner congruence; composite formers component-wise (Step 2b). The precise sibling of the picker-view engine:typeSubsumes (which is collapse(subsetW True))."
@tags "engine" "containment" "subset" "subtype" "phase-6"
subset : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
subset have want = subsetW false have want

-- subsetB — the Bool boundary helper (Nothing → false) for callers that want a
-- clean `if`, the isSubsetB / mGet precedent (C-1).
@label "Subset of types (Bool)"
@description "Phase 6 Step 2 — the Bool-collapsed boundary helper over subset (Nothing → false), for callers that need a clean Bool rather than a Tri (the isSubsetB / decideSubsetB precedent, C-1). subsetB have want = mGet (subset have want) false."
@tags "engine" "containment" "subset" "subtype" "phase-6"
subsetB : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Boolean
subsetB have want = case subset have want of
  Just b -> b
  Nothing -> false

-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- conformable — array SHAPE-CONFORMANCE as a Tri (array-substrate Phase 4, THE
-- CRUX). The containment-family member for TOTAL arrays: `Vec n a = $map (Fin n)
-- a` is a TOTAL function `Fin n → a`, so two arrays CONFORM iff their index
-- domains are EQUAL (not merely ⊆) and the values are covariant. design/array-
-- substrate.md § 2b: `ssMap` decides the key axis as `K1 ⊆ K2` (partial-
-- dictionary — `Vec 3 <: Vec 4 ⇒ Just true`, WRONG for total arrays); conformance
-- flips the key axis to EQUALITY (`K1 ⊆ K2 ∧ K2 ⊆ K1` = `set:decideSubset` BOTH
-- directions) while keeping the value axis covariant (the § 2a free covariance).
--
-- A containment-family DECIDER (sibling of `subset`/`empty`/`disjoint`), NOT a new
-- typeclass: `subset` has no `Subsettable` class, and conformance is its sibling
-- over the same marshalled `TraversalType` — a bespoke `Conformable` class would be
-- the special-case anti-pattern (subsumption directive). It still DISPATCHES, not
-- branches (the § 7 fence): it routes on `tsKind` (the marshalled-shape dispatch
-- `subsetW` uses) and the shape comparison is `decideSubset` (the decider), NEVER a
-- hand-rolled `if length==`. A bare `{$map:…}` TYPE value carries no `$tag`, so a
-- value-dispatched class method could never fire (the Phase-1a/Phase-2 marshal-
-- boundary fact that turned `zip2` into a driver) — the decider is the right tool.
-- Seam: `dispatchedConformable` (engine-bodies-dispatch.ts, the `dispatchedSubset`
-- mirror — an additive arm of the ledgered `$`-key marshal exception).
@label "Conformable types (array shape-conformance)"
@description "array-substrate Phase 4 — `conformable have want` decides whether two array TYPES conform (a Tri): the KEY/index domains are EQUAL (`decideSubset` BOTH directions — total-array equality, not the partial-dictionary `⊆` ssMap uses) AND the values are covariant (`subsetW` one direction). `$opaque`-transparent (peels the `Array` wrapper to the inner `$map`). Non-map shapes (scalars) fall to mutual-subset congruence. The containment-family member for total arrays; the sound `Nothing` surfaces honest undecidability (treated as non-conformant at a hard boundary). design/array-substrate.md § 2b."
@tags "engine" "containment" "conformable" "array" "phase-4"
conformable : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
conformable have want =
  if eq (tsKind have) "opaque" then conformable (tsPure have) want
  else if eq (tsKind want) "opaque" then conformable have (tsPure want)
  else if eq (tsKind have) "map" then conformableMapArm have want
  else conformCongruent have want

@label "conformable: map arm"
@description "array-substrate Phase 4 — the `$map`/array arm of `conformable`: both sides must be `$map`-shaped, then `conformMap`; a map-vs-non-map ⇒ Just false (a kind mismatch — an array does not conform to a scalar/record). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "conformable" "array" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
conformableMapArm : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
conformableMapArm have want =
  if eq (tsKind want) "map" then conformMap have want else Just false

@label "conformable: conformMap"
@description "array-substrate Phase 4 — the total-array conformance rule: key/index EQUALITY (`decideSubset (keys have) (keys want)` AND the reverse — mutual subset = equality, the § 2b headline; `Vec 3` vs `Vec 4` fails here while the partial-dictionary `ssMap` would pass `Vec 3 <: Vec 4`) ∧ covariant values (`subsetW` over the value types). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "conformable" "array" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
conformMap : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
conformMap have want =
  let keysEqual = mAnd (decideSubset (tsMapKeys have) (tsMapKeys want)) (decideSubset (tsMapKeys want) (tsMapKeys have))
  let valsSub = subsetW false (tsMapValues have) (tsMapValues want)
  mAnd keysEqual valsSub

@label "conformable: scalar congruence"
@description "array-substrate Phase 4 — the non-map (scalar / rank-0 `Array [] a = a`, or any other shape) arm of `conformable`: mutual subset (`subsetW` both directions = type equality). A scalar conforms only to an equal scalar type. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "conformable" "array" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
conformCongruent : (have: a) -> (want: a) -> Maybe Boolean
conformCongruent have want =
  mAnd (subsetW false have want) (subsetW false want have)

-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- empty — ⟦t⟧ = ∅ ?  (Tri = Just true | Just false | Nothing)
-- The containment relation's UNARY member (Step 3) — "is this type
-- uninhabited?". The thesis (a type denotes the SET of its inhabitants) makes
-- type-emptiness literally set-emptiness: `empty` self-reasons the structural
-- frame (void ⇒ empty; product ⇒ any-factor-empty; sum ⇒ all-cases-empty; …)
-- and calls the already-Fenel `set:decideEmpty` (resolved as bare `decideEmpty`
-- via the decideEmptySlice harness, engine-bodies-dispatch.ts) at the refinement
-- leaves — the same structural→predicate seam as `subset`/`disjoint`. Completes
-- the subset/disjoint/empty trio Phase 7 (first-class Boolean type formers; `$none`
-- IS the type whose `empty` is Just true) + the prover's PropEmpty/PropInhabited
-- are built on. Step-0 probe verdict: notes/phase-6-step3-step0-probe.md.
--
-- ── The voidVar flag (`emptyW vv`) — the `subsetW picker` trick, for μ ──────
-- `μX. F[X]` is empty ⟺ `F[Void]` is empty (least fixpoint over well-founded
-- ADTs: substituting ⊥ kills the recursive occurrences, leaving the base cases).
-- A `.fenel` body cannot AUTHOR `{$void}` (the `$`-barrier), so instead of a
-- substitution mechanism we thread a Bool `vv`: the `mu` arm flips it on
-- (`emptyW true (tsMuBody t)`), and a bound type-VAR seen under `vv` is treated
-- as Void (⇒ Just true). SOUND AND COMPLETE for well-founded ADTs; resolves
-- Generic Result/ADT emptiness falls through to that rule.  Runtime List is
-- different: its live witness is the host array `[]`, not the pure `Nil` tagged
-- constructor.  The opaque/immediate-μ arms therefore recognize only the exact
-- validation List grammar and certify `Just false` only when its eager element
-- plan is ready; everything else retains the ordinary recursive rule below.
--
-- ── Soundness invariant (the gate for every arm) ────────────────────────────
-- `empty t = Just true ⇒ ⟦t⟧ = ∅` provably; `Just false ⇒ ⟦t⟧` provably
-- inhabited; `Nothing` = undecided. The type-level lift of the `decideEmpty`
-- soundness law. When in doubt, `Nothing` — never guess.
-- ⚠ THAT IS THE INVARIANT, NOT A CLAIM ABOUT HEAD. The register
-- (`design/tcb-ledger.md`) carries live UNSOUND-KNOWN rows reachable from this
-- function — `t.emp.named-atoms` (`empty({$ref:"ℝ"})` = `Just false` while
-- validation refuses every ℝ value, exported through `anyEmptyT` / `emptyUnion`
-- / the top-cover transit); `t.top.opaque` is reachable too but is
-- SIDE-CONDITIONED rather than UNSOUND-KNOWN (round 10). An earlier version of this
-- comment said "Every arm is SOUND", which is a claim about the CODE rather
-- than about the invariant, and it was false. The refined arm (emptyRefined)
-- is the one place the brief's literal rule was corrected — see its comment +
-- notes/phase-6-step3-step0-probe.md §4.
-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Empty (uninhabited) type"
@description "set-algebra-to-fenel Phase 6 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — structural Tri emptiness. Record products and ordinary/exact variant sums pass their complete face gates before structural verdicts. Exact validation-recognized runtime Lists are inhabited by `[]` when their eager element plan is ready, through the narrow opaque/immediate-mu arms; non-Lists retain ordinary recursion."
@tags "engine" "containment" "empty" "uninhabited" "phase-6"
empty : (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
empty t = emptyW false t

@label "empty: emptyW"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — the voidVar-threaded structural-recursive core of empty: a bound type-VAR under vv (set only inside a μ body) ⇒ Just true (the recursive occurrence is Void in the fixpoint check); $void ⇒ Just true; else dispatch on the kind via emptyK. emptyW false is the top-level `empty` (a free var is UNDECIDABLE ⇒ Nothing). Internal core."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyW : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyW vv t =
  if tsIsVar t then emptyVar vv
  else if tsIsVoid t then Just true
  else emptyK vv t (tsKind t)

@label "empty: emptyVar"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — the type-variable arm of emptyW: a bound var seen under the voidVar flag ⇒ Just true (treated as Void in a μ fixpoint); a free var (vv false, top level) ⇒ Nothing (its denotation is unknown ⇒ undecidable). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyVar : (vv: Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyVar vv = if vv then Just true else Nothing

@label "empty: emptyK"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 / type-substrate P1(a.6) / type-substrate P1(a.8) — kind dispatch after var/void: refined retains its recursive rule; **tagged now ABSTAINS unconditionally** (its recursion into the value slot was a verdict across the two live faces' disagreement about what a `$tagged` denotes — ledger `t.emp.tagged`, the emptiness twin of `t.sub.tagged`; MEASURED at P1(a.8) entry, `empty($tagged{value=$void})` = `Just true` while `validate($tagged{value=$void}, <uuid>)` is VALID); opaque and immediate-mu first recognize the exact validation List grammar and otherwise recurse normally. Remaining forms enter emptyKC."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyK : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> (k: String) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyK vv t k =
  if eq k "refined" then emptyRefined vv (tsBase t) (tsRefinedSet t)
  else if eq k "opaque" then emptyOpaqueFace vv t
  else if eq k "mu" then emptyMuFace vv t
  else if eq k "tagged" then Nothing
  else emptyKC vv t k

@label "empty: opaque face"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.6) — carrier-honest opaque emptiness. An exact validation-recognized List uses the live-array witness rule; every other opaque recursively exposes its pure type exactly as before. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "type-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyOpaqueFace : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyOpaqueFace vv t = case validationListInner t of
  Just _elem -> emptyLiveList t
  Nothing -> emptyW vv (tsPure t)

@label "empty: mu face"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.6) — carrier-honest immediate-mu emptiness. An exact validation-recognized List uses the live-array witness rule; every other mu retains the least-fixpoint voidVar recursion. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "type-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyMuFace : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyMuFace vv t = case validationListInner t of
  Just _elem -> emptyLiveList t
  Nothing -> emptyW true (tsMuBody t)

@label "empty: live List"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.6) — exact runtime-List inhabitance: `[]` is a witness on both validation and matchesShape faces, so a validation-recognized List is Just false when its eager element plan is ready. Occurrence readiness is deliberately irrelevant because the empty array has no element occurrences; an unready element plan abstains. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "list" "type-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyLiveList : (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyLiveList t = if ttValidationPlanReady t then Just false else Nothing

-- containment-substrate Phase 2 Step 1b — the tier-2 former arms added to the
-- emptyKC chain below. Union ⇒ ALL branches empty (mAnd; ∪ empty iff every branch
-- is). Intersect ⇒ ANY branch empty OR a provably-disjoint pair (= the
-- `empty (Intersect[A,B]) ≡ disjoint A B` rule; refined-leaf disjoint via
-- ttDisjoint → decideDisjoint). Complement delegates to the shared exact
-- ttTopCover(ttNnf inner) presentation. The arms stay single-line — the explanatory
-- comment lives HERE, not inside the chain (the Fenel-bodied parser fences a
-- comment interrupting an else-if chain).
@label "empty: emptyKC"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — composite emptiness tail: records enter the single-product face gate before anyEmpty; variants enter the whole-variant unique/discriminator/payload gate before allCasesEmpty; tuples remain structural. **P1(a.8): map is now the reading-invariant rule behind its well-formed-card and plan-readiness gates (`t.emp.map`, `t.map.wellformed-card`), arrow is factor-gated (`t.emp.arrow`), and the tagged tail abstains (`t.emp.tagged`).** Boolean formers, named and unknown tails retain their existing rules."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyKC : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> (k: String) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyKC vv t k =
  if eq k "record" then emptyRecordFace vv t
  else if eq k "variant" then emptyVariantFace vv t
  else if eq k "tuple" then anyEmptyT vv (tsTupleItems t)
  else if eq k "map" then emptyMapFace vv t
  else if eq k "arrow" then emptyArrow vv t
  else emptyKF vv t k

@category "engine-internal"
emptyRecordFace : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyRecordFace vv t = anyEmpty vv (tsRecordFields t)

@category "engine-internal"
emptyVariantFace : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyVariantFace vv t =
  if ttVariantSingleReady t then allCasesEmpty vv (tsVariantCases t) else Nothing

@label "empty: emptyMapFace"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.8) — map emptiness, READING-INVARIANT and twice gated. Replaces `emptyKC`'s unconditional `Just false`, which was a false definite: `empty(Vec 3 Void)` claimed INHABITED while ⟦Vec 3 Void⟧ = ∅ under the TOTAL denotation the repo commits to in three places, including this judgment's OWN projection (type-to-set.fenel:231 — \"the canonical JSON-Logic predicate for a TOTAL Fin n map: exact length\"). GATE 1, WELL-FORMEDNESS (`ttWellFormedMapCard`, ledger `t.map.wellformed-card`): a claimed finite card no host array length can satisfy admits no verdict at all. GATE 2, PLAN READINESS: the EXISTING ledgered `ttValidationPlanReady` (`t.sub.plan-ready-gate`) applied to the VALUE type — deliberately the same readiness doctrine rather than a second one, and deliberately at the FACE so NEITHER clause can lift a verdict over a value type validation does not plan. Two independent measured witnesses forced gate 2 to sit here rather than on the keys-empty clause alone: (i) `validationTypePlanError` descends `VtMap.values` UNCONDITIONALLY before any value is examined (validate.fenel:1082, run first at :1583), so a catalog-registered name with a malformed body makes `validate(Vec 0 <name>, [])` INVALID while `empty` said `Just false`; and (ii) `emptyNamed`'s hardcoded tower is WIDER than `validationPrimitiveName`, so `notEmpty` can be `Just true` from a table for a name whose live plan validation resolves from the registry and may refuse — the values-inhabited clause is the same lift, not a safe sibling. Ledger `t.emp.map`. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "map" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyMapFace : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyMapFace vv t =
  if not (ttWellFormedMapCard (tsMapCanonicalKeys t)) then Nothing
  else if not (ttValidationPlanReady (tsMapValues t)) then Nothing
  else emptyMapAgreed vv t

@label "empty: emptyMapAgreed"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.8) — the two clauses on which the PARTIAL-dictionary and TOTAL-function readings of `$map` AGREE, and nothing else. (1) a provably EMPTY key domain ⇒ `Just false`: the unique empty function IS the empty dictionary, so the map is inhabited under both readings. (2) a provably INHABITED value type ⇒ `Just false`: a constant function inhabits under the total reading and `{}` witnesses the partial one. There is NO `Just true` clause and there may never be one — proving a map EMPTY is precisely the claim the partial reading denies, so a `Just true` here would be a false definite under a documented reading. Everything else abstains. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "map" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyMapAgreed : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyMapAgreed vv t =
  if containmentProven (decideEmpty (tsMapCanonicalKeys t)) then Just false
  else if containmentProven (notEmpty vv (tsMapValues t)) then Just false
  else Nothing

@label "empty: ttWellFormedMapCard"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.8) — WELL-FORMEDNESS of a map's key card: can any host value satisfy the card this type CLAIMS? This is NOT a readiness predicate (which asks whether validation holds an eager plan); the distinction is the answer to the review objection that the phase was minting a second trusted readiness doctrine. An OPEN key domain — one neither recogniser reads as finite, including a symbolic `{$expr}` bound — claims no card and is well-formed by default; the gate bites only where a FINITE card is claimed. It is nonetheless a NEW trusted predicate with its own ledger row and its own DISCRIMINATES pin. Why it is needed: `validationFiniteMapCard` (validate.fenel:787) accepts ANY numeric exclusive upper bound with no Nat check, so `$map [0,-1) Number` is recognised as a finite map whose key domain is PROVABLY EMPTY (`decideEmpty` MEASURED `Just true`) — without this gate the keys-empty clause would call it inhabited while validation refuses every value for it. Ledger `t.map.wellformed-card`. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "map" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
ttWellFormedMapCard : (keys: a) -> Boolean
ttWellFormedMapCard keys = case ttFiniteMapCard keys of
  Nothing -> true
  Just n -> ttHostArrayLength n

@label "empty: ttHostArrayLength"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.8) — is this number a card a host array length can actually take? Integral, and in [0, 2^32 − 1]. \"Is it a Nat?\" is NOT sufficient and this is MEASURED: `empty(Vec 4294967296 Number)` was `Just false` at entry while no JavaScript array reaches length 2^32 (the maximum is 2^32 − 1), so the type is uninhabited at the live face while the judgment called it inhabited. NaN and ±∞ are rejected by the RANGE test (NaN fails every comparison), not by the integrality test, so the conjunct order is load-bearing whatever a structural `eq` does with NaN. `-0` passes as card 0, which agrees with validation's `length == -0`. The condition is HOST-REALIZABLE, not mathematically natural. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "map" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
ttHostArrayLength : (n: a) -> Boolean
ttHostArrayLength n =
  and (isNumber n) (and (gte n 0) (and (lte n 4294967295) (eq n (floor n))))

@label "empty: ttFiniteMapCard"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.8) — the finite card a CANONICAL key SetExpr claims, if any. Mirrors `validationFiniteMapCard` (validate.fenel:787) clause for clause, deliberately including its permissiveness: RECOGNITION must match the face, and the WELL-FORMEDNESS judgment is made separately by `ttHostArrayLength`. A stricter recognition here would make the judgment reason about a different type than the one validation checks, which is the defect shape this phase exists to remove. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "map" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
ttFiniteMapCard : (keys: a) -> Maybe Number
ttFiniteMapCard keys = case keys of
  SeInterval { interval = interval } -> ttFiniteMapCardLo interval
  _ -> Nothing

@category "engine-internal"
ttFiniteMapCardLo : (interval: a) -> Maybe Number
ttFiniteMapCardLo interval = case interval.lo of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just lo -> ttFiniteMapCardHi lo interval.hi

@category "engine-internal"
ttFiniteMapCardHi : (lo: a) -> (hi: a) -> Maybe Number
ttFiniteMapCardHi lo hi = case hi of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just h ->
    if and (eq lo.value 0) (and lo.inclusive (and (isNumber h.value) (not h.inclusive)))
    then Just h.value
    else Nothing

@label "empty: tsMapCanonicalKeys"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.8) — the CANONICAL key SetExpr of a TtMap. Deliberately NOT the raw `keys` slot: validation canonicalises before it recognises a finite card (`validationCanonicalSet`, validate.fenel:889) and BOTH slots are marshalled, so a judgment rule reading `keys` and a face reading the canonical form can disagree about the same type. Else passthrough. Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "map" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
tsMapCanonicalKeys : (t: a) -> b
tsMapCanonicalKeys t = case t of
  TtMap { canonicalKeys = k } -> k
  _ -> t

@label "empty: emptyKF"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b / floor-kernel Phase 3c / decide-substrate 8λ.1-r — the tier-2 former tail of emptyKC: union ⇒ all branches empty; intersect ⇒ an empty branch or disjoint pair; complement ⇒ ttTopCover(ttNnf inner), the shared exact top-equivalence presentation; named ⇒ emptyNamed; else Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyKF : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> (k: String) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyKF vv t k =
  if eq k "union" then emptyUnion vv (tsUnionBranches t)
  else if eq k "intersect" then emptyIntersect vv (tsIntersectBranches t)
  else if eq k "complement" then ttTopCover (ttNnf (tsComplementInner t))
  else if eq k "named" then emptyNamed (tsName t)
  else Nothing

@label "empty: emptyNamed"
@description "decide-substrate 8λ.1-r — the named-atom inhabitance arm of emptyKF: the KNOWN atom tower (Number/Int/ℤ/Nat/ℕ/**ℝ**/String/Boolean/Bool/Char) ⇒ Just false (claimed decidably NONempty); any other name (a registered entity could be Void-like) ⇒ Nothing (the closed-world abstention). ⚠ **TWO CORRECTIONS, type-substrate P1(a.8) review round 9.** (i) The list here OMITTED ℝ while the body has always returned `Just false` for it, so the \"any other name ⇒ Nothing\" half was false for exactly the name the filing is about. (ii) \"Inhabited BY CONSTRUCTION\" is the claim `t.emp.named-atoms` FILES AS UNSOUND-KNOWN: the tower is WIDER than `validationPrimitiveName`, and ordinary validation refuses every sampled value for ℤ / ℕ / ℝ / Bool — so for those names the `Just false` is a false definite, exported through `anyEmptyT`, `emptyUnion` and the top-cover transit. Read the tower as a TABLE this arm trusts, not as a proof. The widening that lets emptyArrow certify param-inhabitance — pre-8λ.1-r `empty((Int)→Void)` was Nothing because paramsInhab(Int) couldn't decide, which ALSO meant the arrowSub emptiness gate could never certify a nonempty have ⇒ every arity refutation would have softened. The 8λ.1-r widening was `Nothing→Just false` only — which is monotone in the WIDENING direction but NOT a soundness argument, and the sentence that used to end here (\"Strictly-better … on definitionally-inhabited names\") is RETRACTED: `t.emp.named-atoms` files exactly that claim as a live defect, and `empty({$ref:\"ℝ\"}) = Just false` while ordinary validation refuses the sampled ℝ values. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "decide-substrate" "phase-8lambda"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyNamed : (name: String) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyNamed name =
  if eq name "Number" then Just false
  else if eq name "Int" then Just false
  else if eq name "ℤ" then Just false
  else if eq name "Nat" then Just false
  else if eq name "ℕ" then Just false
  else if eq name "ℝ" then Just false
  else if eq name "String" then Just false
  else if eq name "Boolean" then Just false
  else if eq name "Bool" then Just false
  else if eq name "Char" then Just false
  else Nothing

-- emptyRefined — the refined leaf (⟦base⟧ ∩ S). SOUND CORRECTION to the brief's
-- literal `mOr (emptyW base) (decideEmpty set)`: forward ONLY decideEmpty's
-- Just-TRUE empty-proof (via emTrueOnly: Just false → Nothing). Just true is
-- soundly provable from EITHER base-empty OR set-empty; but base-inhabited AND
-- set-non-empty does NOT imply the intersection inhabited (they can be DISJOINT —
-- the Nat ∩ {<0} gap), so decideEmpty's Just false must NOT be forwarded as a
-- refined inhabited-claim. Strictly sound; never proves a refined type inhabited
-- (a recorded completeness cost — no consumer needs it). See probe §4.
@label "empty: emptyRefined"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — the refined leaf of emptyK: the refined type denotes base ∩ S. SOUND rule (corrects the brief): mOr (emptyW vv base) (emTrueOnly (decideEmpty set)) — Just true from base-empty OR set-empty; emTrueOnly drops decideEmpty's Just false (base-inhabited ∧ set-non-empty does NOT imply the intersection inhabited — the Nat ∩ {<0} disjoint-refinement gap). decideEmpty resolves to set:decideEmpty via the decideEmptySlice harness. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyRefined : (vv: Boolean) -> (base: a) -> (setv: b) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyRefined vv base setv = mOr (emptyW vv base) (emTrueOnly (decideEmpty setv))

@label "empty: emTrueOnly"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — forward ONLY a Tri's positive empty-proof: Just true ⇒ Just true, Just false ⇒ Nothing (drop the inhabited-claim), Nothing ⇒ Nothing. The soundness gate on the decideEmpty arm of emptyRefined (a decideEmpty Just false over a refined base is not a sound refined-inhabited proof). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
emTrueOnly : (m: Maybe Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
emTrueOnly m = case m of
  Just b -> if b then Just true else Nothing
  Nothing -> Nothing

-- ── Kleene OR over Tri (the dual of mAnd) — Just true dominates ──────────────
@label "empty: mOr"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — Kleene disjunction over Tri (Maybe Bool): Just true dominates (∨ true = true); Just false ⇒ the other; Nothing ⇒ Nothing unless the other is Just true. The dual of mAnd; the product (record/tuple) folds' combiner. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
mOr : (a: Maybe Boolean) -> (b: Maybe Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
mOr a b = case a of
  Just av -> if av then Just true else b
  Nothing -> mOrNothing b

@label "empty: mOrNothing"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — the Nothing-left case of mOr: Nothing ∨ Just true = Just true (true dominates), else Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
mOrNothing : (b: Maybe Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
mOrNothing b = case b of
  Just bv -> if bv then Just true else Nothing
  Nothing -> Nothing

-- ── record (product) / tuple — empty iff ANY factor empty; empty list inhabits
@label "empty: anyEmpty"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — keyed-product emptiness. The entire product first passes scoped embedded/effective coordinate, eager-plan, reserved-wire, and enforcing-occurrence checks; only then does anyEmptyFold prove emptiness from any empty factor. An empty ready product is inhabited."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
anyEmpty : (vv: Boolean) -> (fs: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
anyEmpty vv fs = if ttProductSingleReady fs "" then anyEmptyFold vv fs else Nothing

@category "engine-internal"
anyEmptyFold : (vv: Boolean) -> (fs: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
anyEmptyFold vv fs = case head fs of
  Nothing -> Just false
  Just f -> mOr (emptyW vv (tsFieldType f)) (anyEmptyFold vv (ssRest fs))

@label "empty: anyEmptyT"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — the tuple (product) emptiness fold: empty iff ANY item type is empty (mOr-fold of emptyW over the bare TtTuple item types); an empty item-list ⇒ Just false. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
anyEmptyT : (vv: Boolean) -> (is: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
anyEmptyT vv is = case head is of
  Nothing -> Just false
  Just i -> mOr (emptyW vv i) (anyEmptyT vv (ssRest is))

-- ── variant (sum) — empty iff ALL cases empty; empty case-list is Void-like ──
@label "empty: allCasesEmpty"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — variant-sum fold reached only after emptyVariantFace's whole-variant gate. All case payloads must be empty; an empty gated case list is Void-like."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
allCasesEmpty : (vv: Boolean) -> (cs: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
allCasesEmpty vv cs = case head cs of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just c -> mAnd (caseEmpty vv c) (allCasesEmpty vv (ssRest cs))

@label "empty: caseEmpty"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 / type-substrate P1(a.6) — one already-whole-gated variant payload, reusing the single-product anyEmpty gate before its factor fold. A ready nullary payload is inhabited."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
caseEmpty : (vv: Boolean) -> (c: a) -> Maybe Boolean
caseEmpty vv c = anyEmpty vv (tsCaseFields c)

-- ── arrow — the INHABITED clauses only (type-substrate P1(a.7)) ─────────────
-- The exponential law still computes: `P1->…->Pn->R` is empty iff `R` is empty
-- AND every param is inhabited.  Only its NEGATIVE half is entitled at the live
-- faces, so only that half is emitted.
--   KEPT (`Just false`, both clauses).  `mAnd`'s false-dominates gives exactly
--   two: R provably NONempty ⇒ constant functions inhabit; some param provably
--   EMPTY ⇒ the vacuous function inhabits.  ⚠ P1(a.7) entitled both on the claim
--   that validation's IMPLEMENTED arrow arm accepts `""` for EVERY arrow type
--   (validate.fenel:1523-1524), so no arrow's face population is empty.  P1(a.8)
--   MEASURED THAT FALSE — `validationRuntime` runs `validationTypePlanError`
--   FIRST and its `VtArrow` arm audits the parameter access plan and the return
--   before that leaf is reached, so an arrow with an unready FACTOR refuses every
--   value, `""` included.  Hence the FACTOR GATE below; the two clauses are
--   emitted only over an arrow whose factors validation can plan.
--   FENCED (`Just true` ⇒ `Nothing`).  `empty((Int)→Void)` is derivable
--   conceptually and FALSE at that same implemented arm, for the same reason:
--   `""` inhabits it.  Two-doctrine agreement is the bar, so the leg abstains.
-- The fence lives HERE rather than at `emptyKC` on purpose: `arrowSub` reads
-- `emptyArrow` directly for its `∅ ⊆ want` short-circuit, and fencing only the
-- `empty` entry point would have left that second emitter live.
-- Blast (measured, all definite → Nothing, never a polarity flip):
-- `empty(((Int)→Void)→Void)` was `Just false` on a vacuity proof that rode the
-- now-fenced inner emptiness and becomes `Nothing`.  ⚠ The sibling claim here —
-- that `empty(((Int)→Void)→Number)` STAYS `Just false` on the independent
-- inhabited-return clause — was true of P1(a.7) and is FALSE at HEAD: P1(a.8)'s
-- factor gate sees an ARROW param, `ttSlotsPlanReady` is unconditionally false
-- for it, and the whole arm abstains.  MEASURED `Nothing` (round 5).  The
-- `recordSubGated` / `variantCaseSub` vacuity rescues are ALREADY dead for
-- arrow-bearing products, because `ttValidationPlanReady` is unconditionally
-- false for `TtArrow` and `ttProductSingleReady` fails first.
@label "empty: emptyArrow"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 / type-substrate P1(a.7) / type-substrate P1(a.8) — the arrow arm, INHABITED-CLAUSES ONLY and now FACTOR-GATED. The exponential law `empty(P1->…->Pn->R) ⟺ empty(R) ∧ every param inhabited` still computes, but only its Just false half is emitted: R provably nonempty ⇒ constant functions inhabit, and some param provably empty ⇒ the vacuous function inhabits. P1(a.7) entitled those two clauses on the claim that `validationValidateArrow` accepts the empty string for EVERY arrow type, so no arrow's live population is empty. **P1(a.8) MEASURED that claim FALSE.** `validationRuntime` runs `validationTypePlanError` FIRST (validate.fenel:1583), and its `VtArrow` arm audits the parameter ACCESS PLAN and then the return (`:1095-1101`) before `validationValidateArrow` is ever reached — so a factor whose plan validation cannot hold makes the arrow refuse every value, `\"\"` included. Witness: `empty(({$ref:<catalog name with a duplicate semantic field key>}) -> Number)` = `Just false` at entry while `validate(…, \"\")` is INVALID. The gate is `ttSlotsPlanReady` over the PARAMS (the slot predicate, not a per-param TYPE fold — validation audits identity/projection as well as type) and `ttValidationPlanReady` over the RETURN: the same ledgered readiness doctrine (`t.sub.plan-ready-gate`) the record arm already uses, applied to the factors the preflight actually visits. This is a same-shape sibling of the map repair, found by design review and repaired at the source rather than masked by the map gate. The Just true (empty) leg remains fenced. Fenced inside this function, not at emptyKC, because arrowSub reads it directly for its empty-have short-circuit. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyArrow : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyArrow vv t =
  if not (ttArrowFactorsPlanReady t) then Nothing
  else emptyArrowInhabited vv t

@label "empty: emptyArrowInhabited"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.8) — the retained inhabited half of the exponential law, reached only through `emptyArrow`'s factor gate. Split out so the gate is a separate, revertible clause with its own DISCRIMINATES pin. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyArrowInhabited : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyArrowInhabited vv t = case mAnd (emptyW vv (tsArrowReturns t)) (paramsInhab vv (tsArrowParams t)) of
  Just false -> Just false
  _ -> Nothing

@label "empty: ttArrowFactorsPlanReady"
@description "type-substrate P1(a.8) — every factor validation's eager preflight visits for an arrow: the parameter ACCESS PLAN (`ttSlotsPlanReady`, which checks slot identity and current-wire projection as well as each param's own readiness — a per-param TYPE fold would miss the identity half) and the RETURN type (`ttValidationPlanReady`). Mirrors `validationTypePlanError`'s `VtArrow` arm (validate.fenel:1095-1101). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "type-substrate" "phase-1a8"
@category "engine-internal"
ttArrowFactorsPlanReady : (t: a) -> Boolean
ttArrowFactorsPlanReady t =
  and (ttSlotsPlanReady (tsArrowParams t)) (ttValidationPlanReady (tsArrowReturns t))

@label "empty: paramsInhab"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — the all-params-inhabited Kleene-AND fold for emptyArrow: mAnd-fold of notEmpty over the TtArrowParam types; an empty param-list ⇒ Just true (vacuous ⇒ a thunk ()->R is empty iff R is). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
paramsInhab : (vv: Boolean) -> (ps: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
paramsInhab vv ps = case head ps of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just p -> mAnd (notEmpty vv (tsParamType p)) (paramsInhab vv (ssRest ps))

@label "empty: notEmpty"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — `is this type inhabited?` as a Tri = the negation of emptyW (neg3): Just true ⇒ provably inhabited, Just false ⇒ provably empty, Nothing ⇒ undecided. Used by paramsInhab. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
notEmpty : (vv: Boolean) -> (t: a) -> Maybe Boolean
notEmpty vv t = neg3 (emptyW vv t)

@label "empty: neg3"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — Tri (Maybe Bool) negation: Just b ⇒ Just (not b), Nothing ⇒ Nothing. Internal helper (avoids std:not — inlines the flip)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
neg3 : (m: Maybe Boolean) -> Maybe Boolean
neg3 m = case m of
  Just b -> if b then Just false else Just true
  Nothing -> Nothing

-- ── tagged value-slot accessor ──────────────────────────────────────────────
-- `Id<X>`: the value slot is the inhabitance-bearing one UNDER THE VALUE-RECURSION
-- reading.  P1(a.8) fenced every SOUND-mode consumer of that reading, because the
-- live validation face admits exactly the UUID strings whatever the slot holds.
-- The accessor survives for the PICKER arms, which are a presentation filter.
@label "empty: tsTaggedValue"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 / type-substrate P1(a.8) — the value type of a TtTagged. It is the inhabitance-bearing slot UNDER THE VALUE-RECURSION READING ONLY (the phantom is type-level provenance); the live validation face admits exactly the UUID strings whatever the slot holds, which is why P1(a.8) fenced every SOUND-mode consumer of this accessor and left it serving the PICKER arms, a presentation filter. Carried by marshalTraversalType (engine-bodies-dispatch.ts). Else passthrough. Internal accessor."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsTaggedValue : (t: a) -> a
tsTaggedValue t = case t of
  TtTagged { value = v } -> v
  _ -> t

@label "empty: tsIsVoid"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — is the marshalled type a TtVoid ($void, uninhabited)? Internal helper (tsKind has no void case ⇒ checked directly in emptyW)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-6"
@category "engine-internal"
tsIsVoid : (t: a) -> Boolean
tsIsVoid t = case t of
  TtVoid -> True
  _ -> False

-- ── Step 1b — the tier-2 former emptiness folds ─────────────────────────────

@label "empty: emptyUnion"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — the union (∪) emptiness fold: a union is empty iff ALL branches are empty (mAnd-fold of emptyW over the TtUnion branches). An empty branch list ⇒ Just true (∪∅ = ∅). Sound AND complete. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyUnion : (vv: Boolean) -> (branches: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyUnion vv branches = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Just true
  Just b -> mAnd (emptyW vv b) (emptyUnion vv (ssRest branches))

@label "empty: emptyIntersect"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — the intersect (∩) emptiness fold: empty iff ANY branch is provably empty OR some pair of branches is provably disjoint (= the `empty (Intersect[A,B]) ≡ disjoint A B` rule). mOr of intersectAnyEmpty (any-branch-empty, emTrueOnly so a non-empty branch never refutes) and intersectAnyDisjoint (pairwise ttDisjoint over refined leaves). SOUND: only emits Just true on a genuine proof; else Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
emptyIntersect : (vv: Boolean) -> (branches: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
emptyIntersect vv branches = mOr (intersectAnyEmpty vv branches) (intersectAnyDisjoint branches)

@label "empty: intersectAnyEmpty"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — the any-branch-empty arm of emptyIntersect: Just true if SOME branch is provably empty, else Nothing (emTrueOnly drops each branch's Just false — all-branches-non-empty does NOT prove the intersection inhabited). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
intersectAnyEmpty : (vv: Boolean) -> (branches: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
intersectAnyEmpty vv branches = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b -> mOr (emTrueOnly (emptyW vv b)) (intersectAnyEmpty vv (ssRest branches))

@label "empty: intersectAnyDisjoint"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — the pairwise-disjoint arm of emptyIntersect: Just true if SOME pair of branches is provably disjoint (via ttDisjoint → decideDisjoint over refined leaves), else Nothing. Two disjoint branches ⇒ the intersection is empty. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
intersectAnyDisjoint : (branches: List a) -> Maybe Boolean
intersectAnyDisjoint branches = case head branches of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b -> mOr (intersectDisjointAgainst b (ssRest branches)) (intersectAnyDisjoint (ssRest branches))

@label "empty: intersectDisjointAgainst"
@description "Phase 2 Step 1b — is the branch `b` provably disjoint from any LATER branch? mOr-fold of emTrueOnly(ttDisjoint b o) over the rest (each Just false dropped — proven-non-disjoint is not a positive emptiness proof). Internal helper to intersectAnyDisjoint."
@tags "engine" "internal" "containment" "empty" "phase-2"
@category "engine-internal"
intersectDisjointAgainst : (b: a) -> (others: List c) -> Maybe Boolean
intersectDisjointAgainst b others = case head others of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just o -> mOr (emTrueOnly (ttDisjoint b o)) (intersectDisjointAgainst b (ssRest others))

-- emptyB — the Bool boundary helper (Nothing → false) for callers that want a
-- clean `if`, the subsetB / isSubsetB / mGet precedent (C-1).
@label "Empty type (Bool)"
@description "Phase 6 Step 3 — the Bool-collapsed boundary helper over empty (Nothing → false), for callers that need a clean Bool rather than a Tri (the subsetB / decideSubsetB precedent, C-1). emptyB t = mGet (empty t) false."
@tags "engine" "containment" "empty" "uninhabited" "phase-6"
emptyB : (t: a) -> Boolean
emptyB t = case empty t of
  Just b -> b
  Nothing -> false
